    "bodyMarkdown": "# Block Out! - Color Sort Puzzle: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nBlock Out! builds its color puzzle around moving blocks to matching doors, then complicates that familiar objective with elevators and generators.\n\n## Doors are destinations, not just decorations\n\nThe basic action is sliding a colored block toward its corresponding exit. Clearing a block opens room for later moves, so the objective is also a space-management problem. A block that is close to its door may still be less urgent than one obstructing several other routes.\n\nThe listing singles out moving elevators and block generators. These additions distinguish the pitch from a completely static sliding puzzle: you are planning around mechanisms as well as the pieces already present. Their exact schedules and constraints are not described, so there is no basis for prescribing a universal solution sequence.\n\nThat uncertainty is especially relevant to the pacing. The play guide tells you both to position blocks carefully and to move faster. It presents strategy and action as a combination, rather than promising an entirely leisurely experience. Readers who dislike pressure should not interpret the bright colors as proof that every level is untimed.\n\n## Where the design could appeal\n\nThe clearest audience is a player who likes clearing congested boards but wants more than a sequence of fixed obstacles. Generators suggest that managing what enters the board may matter alongside removing what is already there. Elevators suggest that access can change instead of remaining permanently open or closed. These are design implications of the advertised mechanisms, not observations of later levels.\n\nIf your favorite puzzles depend on seeing all pieces and constraints from the start, the dynamic elements are a reason to inspect the game more carefully. If changing layouts are what keep sliding puzzles interesting for you, they are the main reason to consider it.\n\n## Free access and missing details\n\nThe US listing offers a free download and advertises offline play. It does not, in the supplied description, establish the frequency of ads, any removal offer, or what happens after a failed level. Offline marketing is not a substitute for checking those systems. No customer review sample is available here to resolve them.\n\n## Verdict\n\nConsider Block Out! for sliding-block routing with active board mechanisms. Its distinguishing idea is the elevator-and-generator combination; its tolerance for slow, careful solving remains a practical question.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What do you do in Block Out!?\n\nSlide colored blocks to matching doors while managing limited board space and additional mechanisms.\n\n### Does it have elevators?\n\nYes. Moving elevators and block generators are explicitly advertised in the listing.\n\n### Is Block Out! ad-free?\n\nThat is not established by the supplied evidence. A free download and an offline claim do not prove ad-free play.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/block-out-color-sort-puzzle/id6752672568?uo=4).",
