    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Tiles - Relaxing Puzzle: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nWord Tiles adds a useful wrinkle to the familiar task of building words: small numbers on the tiles indicate how many times each letter must be used.\n\n## Vocabulary plus a usage budget\n\nYou connect letter tiles to make words and fill empty spaces on the board. The developer calls it a crossword twist, but the most distinctive rule in the description is the count attached to each tile. Finding a valid word is only part of the task; you also need to account for the required uses of its letters.\n\nThat creates a link between word choice and the remaining board. A plausible answer might use letters you still need elsewhere, while a less obvious word could help satisfy the outstanding counts. This is a design implication of the stated usage rule, not a claim about a specific level solution or the game’s dictionary.\n\nThe listing advertises hundreds of levels that become harder. It does not specify the vocabulary range, treatment of proper nouns, or whether alternative valid answers receive credit. Those details matter if your enjoyment of a word game depends on generous word acceptance rather than matching a predetermined set.\n\n## Deliberate solving is the advertised pace\n\nThe developer says there is no timer and that you can play at your own pace. That makes the stated premise a better match for considering letter combinations than for racing through a word search. Calm backgrounds support the intended presentation, but they are not evidence about the size or readability of tile numbers on a particular device.\n\nConsider Word Tiles if you enjoy word construction but want a visible constraint beyond “find any word.” The letter counts give you another source of information when vocabulary alone does not immediately produce an answer. Skip it if you want traditional newspaper clues or a timed competitive vocabulary test; neither is the core pitch here.\n\n## Free download, incomplete economy details\n\nThe saved US download price is free. The description does not establish how hints are obtained, whether advertising interrupts levels, or what paid offers exist. There is no customer sample here to fill those gaps. The no-timer claim should not be expanded into a promise of unrestricted retries, offline access, or free assistance.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Tiles is worth considering for the interaction between word formation and counted letter use. Its most interesting feature is a constraint you can reason about, not the broad promise that a word game keeps your mind sharp.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What do the numbers on Word Tiles mean?\n\nThe description says the small numbers show how many times each letter must be used.\n\n### Is Word Tiles timed?\n\nThe developer explicitly says there is no timer. This has not been independently tested.\n\n### Is it a traditional crossword?\n\nIt uses a crossword-style board, but the listed action is connecting letter tiles to make words rather than answering conventional written clues.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-tiles-relaxing-puzzle/id6783815362?uo=4).",
