    "bodyMarkdown": "# CubeAway - 3DPuzzle: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nCubeAway - 3DPuzzle moves an arrow-removal problem onto six faces of a cube. The advertised objective is to clear every arrow in the correct order.\n\n## The extra dimension is the selling point\n\nThe description presents intertwined arrows arranged across a cube, asking you to anticipate moves and visualize chain reactions. That adds a spatial-reading demand to the more familiar question of which piece can leave first. A face you are focusing on is only part of the described object.\n\nThe text does not supply a complete movement diagram or specify how the camera is controlled. It would therefore be premature to promise free rotation, particular swipe gestures, or a precise rule for arrows crossing edges. What is explicit is that all six sides matter to clearing the cube.\n\nCorrect order is emphasized repeatedly. The developer also asks players to remove arrows without making a mistake, but does not explain whether errors cost lives, restart a stage, or simply stop an action. That distinction will matter to anyone who likes exploring a problem through experimentation.\n\n## Spatial patience rather than a standard number puzzle\n\nThe strongest audience is someone who enjoys mentally tracking how one removal affects access to another. If a flat diagram feels too familiar, the cube presentation offers a clear reason to investigate this version. If changing viewpoints makes a puzzle harder to read rather than more interesting, that same feature may be a drawback.\n\nThe listing mixes calm language with references to timing, precision, and never letting your guard down. Those phrases should not be converted into a claim that the game is untimed or pressure-free. Nor does its simple visual pitch establish accessibility for every screen size or visual need.\n\n## Cost and missing evidence\n\nThe saved US download price is free. The supplied description does not document ad placements, a removal purchase, hint costs, offline support, or a level total. No customer review bodies are available here to establish how players respond to the cube’s readability or difficulty.\n\nThe useful decision is whether six-face spatial sequencing is what you want. There is considerably less evidence for the broader promise of a peaceful experience than for that specific puzzle concept.\n\n## Verdict\n\nCubeAway is a candidate for players who actively want arrow sequencing to involve spatial visualization. Those seeking a fully specified, forgiving ruleset should wait for clearer information about mistakes and movement.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What is the goal in CubeAway?\n\nThe listing says to remove all arrows from the cube in the correct order.\n\n### Are all six faces involved?\n\nYes. The description explicitly asks whether you can clear arrows placed on all six sides.\n\n### Does a mistake restart the level?\n\nThe developer emphasizes avoiding mistakes, but the supplied description does not explain the exact penalty.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cubeaway-3dpuzzle/id6760325543?uo=4).",
