    "bodyMarkdown": "# Fish Sort Puzzle - Bubble Jam: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nFish Sort Puzzle - Bubble Jam makes the aquarium targets more important than the fish theme. Each tank requests a quantity, and fish that do not fit the current targets consume temporary space.\n\n## Collection targets control useful moves\n\nThe listing says to tap fish and send them to new homes. Each aquarium displays the number of fish it needs, and completing a collection requires enough of the appropriate type. This is not simply grouping every fish into any available container.\n\nNonmatching fish go into a temporary holding area. If it fills, the attempt ends. That makes the buffer a real resource: a tap can expose something useful while also reducing your room for future mistakes or necessary detours.\n\nThe board changes as bubbles are cleared below and new ones make way from above. Your larger objective is to eliminate all bubbles and advance. Aquarium requests, the changing supply, and the holding area therefore interact, rather than operating as three unrelated decorations.\n\nThe description is brief enough that several practical rules remain open. It does not specify a holding capacity, how tanks are replaced after completion, or which taps are initially legal. Those details should not be filled in from other color-collection games.\n\n## A fit for readers who like managing a buffer\n\nThe useful appeal is balancing an immediate match against what you need to expose next. If you enjoy making room while fulfilling visible targets, the premise offers a clear reason to inspect the game. If you want unrestricted rearrangement or a pure aquarium simulation, this is not what the listing describes.\n\nThe quantity labels also distinguish the idea from a puzzle where recognizing a pair is enough. You are working toward a requested amount, although the evidence does not establish the eventual size or complexity of those requests.\n\n## Ads, purchases, and pace\n\nThe saved US download price is free. The supplied description does not document advertising, purchase offers, offline operation, or timers. Its cheerful underwater presentation does not answer those questions. Nor does the absence of review bodies establish that players have no complaints.\n\nThe most informative rule is the overflow condition. Prospective players should choose on whether a limited waiting area sounds enjoyable, not on an assumption that tapping fish is automatically consequence-free.\n\n## Verdict\n\nConsider Fish Sort Puzzle for quantity-based collection with a limited buffer. Its aquarium targets give the sorting a clear purpose, but monetization and the finer rules remain underdocumented.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What do the aquarium numbers mean?\n\nThe listing says each aquarium displays how many fish it needs to complete its collection.\n\n### Where do nonmatching fish go?\n\nThey enter a temporary holding area. Filling it ends the attempt, according to the description.\n\n### What clears a level?\n\nThe stated overall goal is to eliminate all bubbles and advance to the next stage.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fish-sort-puzzle-bubble-jam/id6771681639?uo=4).",
