    "bodyMarkdown": "# Merge Bubbles - Word Game: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nMerge Bubbles - Word Game is about relationships between words, not spelling longer ones. Your task is to recognize four members of the same category and bring their bubbles together.\n\n## Meaning supplies the matching rule\n\nEach bubble contains a word. Merge related word bubbles until a group of four completes a category, clears space, and unlocks more bubbles. That makes semantic recognition the main skill: sharing letters or looking alike is not the described requirement.\n\nThe category itself may be hidden at first. You need to identify a common link among the available words, then decide which merges will make useful progress. The description does not supply actual category examples or explain whether ambiguous words can belong to several possible groups, so the vocabulary’s range cannot be judged from the pitch alone.\n\nMore bubbles drop into the level as you advance. Clearing a category therefore changes the available information as well as the space. This distinguishes the concept from a static word list where every candidate is present from the beginning.\n\n## Relaxed presentation, limited moves\n\nThe developer repeatedly calls the game relaxing, but the play guide also warns against exceeding the move count. That is an important boundary. Even without evidence of a countdown, the advertised puzzle does not offer an unlimited number of actions.\n\nA player who likes considering word meanings may appreciate that constraint as a reason to plan before combining. A player who wants to experiment freely with every plausible connection may find it less appealing. The supplied material does not explain undo, penalties for mistaken groups, or assistance tools.\n\n## Audience and spending questions\n\nConsider Merge Bubbles if word associations interest you more than crossword clues or letter searches. It is not pitched as a numeric merge game, despite the familiar bubble-merging imagery. The central objective is completing categories of four.\n\nThe saved US download is free. Ad frequency, purchase prices, offline support, and the cost of extra moves are not established in the supplied description. There are no customer review bodies here to say whether players regard the category connections as clever or arbitrary.\n\nThat last distinction is the essential quality question for this format: a satisfying answer needs a convincing relationship, not merely a matching animation.\n\n## Verdict\n\nMerge Bubbles offers a clear semantic twist on a familiar visual format. Consider it for four-word category recognition, while recognizing that a move budget makes the stated relaxation conditional on careful choices.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### How many words make a category?\n\nThe listing specifies four related words for a completed category.\n\n### Is Merge Bubbles about spelling words?\n\nNo. Each bubble already contains a word; the task is grouping related meanings.\n\n### Are moves limited?\n\nThe play guide explicitly warns players not to exceed the move count. The exact limits and recovery options are not specified.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/merge-bubbles-word-game/id6766297786?uo=4).",
