    "bodyMarkdown": "# Hotel Legacy: Merge Game: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nHotel Legacy: Merge Game starts with an inheritance and builds toward a hotel empire. Alyssa’s grandmother leaves her a Hotel Manor, giving item merging a restoration story and a growing guest list.\n\n## Guests give the items a purpose\n\nThe description presents merging as a way to create food, drinks, souvenirs, and other items for guests. More items become available as you progress. That hospitality theme is the direct connection between the puzzle board and the broader hotel project.\n\nThe listing does not document exact merge-chain lengths, board dimensions, or generation rules. It would be misleading to supply those from other renovation games. What it does establish is that serving guests and expanding the item catalog are central parts of the proposed loop.\n\nRenovation extends beyond a single building. You buy land, restore old structures, and turn them into themed hotels in different places and periods. That gives the advertised progression a wider decorative scope than repairing one room repeatedly, although the number of hotels and the freedom of each design choice are not specified.\n\n## Relationships alongside restoration\n\nAlyssa meets guests from around the world, hears their stories, and forms relationships. Possible romance is also part of the pitch. The attraction is therefore not just improving buildings, but following the people who enter them.\n\nConsider this if you like item progression to lead into renovation and character scenes. It is less suitable if dialogue feels like an interruption to the puzzle or if you want a detailed business simulation. The description does not establish staffing systems, operating budgets, or realistic hotel management despite the empire framing.\n\n## Purchases and unanswered progression questions\n\nThe US download is free, and the listing explicitly discloses optional purchases including random-item purchases or loot boxes. That disclosure is worth noticing before treating the game as a consequence-free decorating diversion. The supplied evidence does not give prices, odds, or a tested no-spend pace.\n\nAdvertising, offline support, energy limits, and wait timers are not documented in the supplied description. There are no saved customer review bodies for this entry to establish whether guests’ orders feel rewarding or restrictive. The recommendation must therefore rest on the hospitality-and-renovation concept rather than invented player sentiment.\n\n## Verdict\n\nHotel Legacy is a candidate for readers who want merging attached to themed properties and guest relationships. The explicit randomized-purchase disclosure is an important caveat, while the actual pacing remains unverified.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Who is Alyssa in Hotel Legacy?\n\nShe is the protagonist who inherits a Hotel Manor from her grandmother and sets out to develop hotels.\n\n### What items do you merge?\n\nThe description names food, drinks, souvenirs, and other guest-service items.\n\n### Does Hotel Legacy contain randomized purchases?\n\nYes. Its description discloses optional random-item purchases or loot boxes.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/hotel-legacy-merge-game/id6752886832?uo=4).",
