    "bodyMarkdown": "# Royal Smash! - Physics Puzzle: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nRoyal Smash! - Physics Puzzle has an unusually short written description. Its official screenshots supply the useful detail: a cannon aimed at stacked objects, with destruction rather than construction as the apparent goal.\n\n## Aim at the structure\n\nThe first saved screenshot shows a red cannon facing a pyramid of blue-and-white cans on a raised platform. The caption reads “Aim, Fire, Destroy!” A castle landscape supplies the royal theme, but the foreground action is a targeted shot at a structure.\n\nThe second image shows a projectile breaking through a colorful tower of container-like blocks above water. Its caption, “One Shot Max Damage,” emphasizes the result of a well-placed hit. These are promotional images, not observations of how a real attempt unfolds.\n\nTogether, the pictures support a more specific description than the generic label physics puzzle: the visible premise is aiming a cannon to knock apart stacked objects. They do not establish the number of shots available in every level, the aiming gesture, or an exact success threshold.\n\n## Precision is advertised; timing is less explained\n\nThe written listing says mastering levels takes precision and timing. It does not explain what must be timed or whether a countdown exists. A claim that every stage is relaxed and untimed would therefore go beyond the evidence, as would inventing moving targets or specific wind effects.\n\nThis looks most relevant to readers who enjoy planning a shot and watching a structure react. It is less clearly suited to someone seeking a fixed-rule deduction puzzle with no action component. The cannon and destructible stacks are the distinctive proposition; the royal theme is the setting around it.\n\n## What you cannot infer from the images\n\nA single-shot caption is not proof that all boards can be completed with one shot or that misses are free to retry. The screenshot explosions also do not establish the accuracy of the physics simulation, frame rate, or tactile feel.\n\nThe US download is listed as free. Advertising, purchase offers, offline access, level count, and recovery after failure are not established by the supplied material. With no saved review bodies, there is no basis for attributing praise or frustration to players. This is a visual listing analysis of a sparse product pitch.\n\n## Verdict\n\nRoyal Smash! is worth considering for cannon-based destruction puzzles, not for an extensively documented ruleset. The official images explain the concept better than the text, while leaving cost and failure conditions unresolved.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What do you do in Royal Smash!?\n\nOfficial screenshots show a cannon aimed at stacked cans or blocks, with captions about aiming and destruction.\n\n### Is every level limited to one shot?\n\nOne screenshot promotes one-shot damage, but a universal shot limit is not established.\n\n### Is Royal Smash! timed?\n\nThe description mentions timing without specifying a countdown or the exact timing mechanic.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/royal-smash-physics-puzzle/id6780891673?uo=4).",
