    "bodyMarkdown": "# Hole Stars: Puzzle Game: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nHole Stars: Puzzle Game turns collecting into a race. Swipe a black hole through a field of objects, grow large enough to take bigger items, and finish before the clock expires.\n\n## Size changes what you can collect\n\nThe description says collecting objects enlarges the hole, allowing it to swallow larger items. That gives the route a progression constraint: the biggest target may not be the first useful destination. Smaller collections build the capacity needed for later objects.\n\nThe board also contains blockers and tricky objects. The listing does not explain every obstacle type, so it would be premature to name specific hazards or prescribe a universal route. What is clear is that movement, growth, and clearance need to work together.\n\nUnlike a tap-to-match puzzle, the advertised control is swiping to move continuously around the level. This makes path selection and execution part of the proposition. The supplied evidence does not establish the precision of the controls or whether the hole can be steered comfortably with one hand.\n\n## The countdown is not optional wording\n\nThe developer repeatedly describes beating the clock and collecting everything before time runs out. This is the central caveat for readers drawn in by the relaxing visuals and ASMR-inspired effects. The game may be presented as soothing, but its stated rules involve time pressure.\n\nBoosters are advertised for difficult situations. Leaderboards and competition with friends add speed-oriented goals beyond simply finishing a board. Neither feature establishes how easy stages are without assistance or whether all competition requires a connected account.\n\n## Audience and spending\n\nConsider Hole Stars if you enjoy planning an efficient collection route and watching size growth unlock larger targets. Skip it if you want a puzzle you can leave untouched while considering a long deduction, or if countdowns are a firm exclusion.\n\nThe saved US download is free. The supplied description does not document booster prices, ad frequency, paid removal, offline access, or failure recovery. There are no saved customer review bodies from which to derive claims about late-game fairness or technical stability.\n\nThe distinctive question is whether racing to enlarge a collector sounds enjoyable. The sound-effects pitch should not distract from that much more consequential design choice.\n\n## Verdict\n\nHole Stars is better understood as timed collection with route planning than as a purely restful sorting game. Consider it for growth and movement; skip it if beating a countdown is exactly what you want to avoid.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### How does the black hole grow?\n\nThe listing says gathering objects enlarges it, allowing larger items to be collected.\n\n### Is Hole Stars timed?\n\nYes. The description repeatedly states that you must collect everything before the clock runs out.\n\n### How do you move the hole?\n\nSwiping is the advertised control. Its responsiveness has not been independently tested.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/hole-stars-puzzle-game/id6747028173?uo=4).",
