    "bodyMarkdown": "# Crossword Go!: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nCrossword Go! puts an opponent on the other side of the word grid. Its pitch is live scoring competition, not quietly finishing a daily newspaper crossword at your own pace.\n\n## Word knowledge is only one part of the score\n\nThe play guide says to draw letters and form high-scoring words on a crossword grid. Long words, combinations, and smart plays earn bonuses. That means placement and scoring choices matter alongside recognizing the answer.\n\nThe developer describes both written hints and picture clues. Those provide different kinds of prompts, potentially making the challenge broader than reading a conventional clue list. The supplied description does not show exactly how picture clues integrate with the grid or how available letters are distributed.\n\nPower-ups are advertised as a way to turn a match in your favor. Their effects, limits, and acquisition costs are not documented. For a competitive word-game reader, that is a meaningful missing detail: a scoring contest involving assists is not automatically comparable to a pure vocabulary test.\n\n## Real-time play changes the audience\n\nThe description repeatedly emphasizes live duels and no waiting. This is a reason to consider the game if you dislike long delays between turns, and a reason to skip it if you want a puzzle you can set aside indefinitely. The evidence does not establish a precise clock length or matchmaking wait time.\n\nDaily challenges and leaderboards provide additional goals. Those features do not prove opponent identity, competitive balance, or a specific progression path. Claims about expanding vocabulary and training the brain are positioning, not demonstrated educational outcomes.\n\n## Costs and connections\n\nThe saved US download is free. Ad frequency, power-up pricing, subscription offers, and the exact access requirements for live matches are not established in the supplied description. The live premise should not be converted into an offline-play promise.\n\nThere are no saved customer review bodies for this entry, so it would be inappropriate to say players find matchmaking fair or complain about a particular exploit. The useful evaluation is conceptual: do you want crossword-style clues to feed a scored, assisted contest rather than a solitary completion goal?\n\nThat distinction is more important than the familiar crossword label when deciding whether this belongs beside your existing word games.\n\n## Verdict\n\nCrossword Go! is a candidate for competitive word players who want live rounds and mixed clue types. Skip it if your preferred crossword experience is untimed solitude or if unexplained power-ups undermine the appeal of scoring.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Is Crossword Go! turn-based?\n\nThe developer emphasizes real-time duels and no waiting rather than asynchronous turns.\n\n### Does it use picture clues?\n\nYes. Both traditional word hints and picture clues are advertised.\n\n### Do power-ups affect matches?\n\nThe description advertises strategic power-ups, but their exact effects and costs are not supplied.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/crossword-go/id6739069151?uo=4).",
