    "bodyMarkdown": "# Color Block Jam: iOS Puzzle Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. Based on the saved US App Store listing; the supplied collection contains no customer review bodies for this game (sample N=0; no review date or version window).*\n\nColor Block Jam is a routing puzzle in which the destination color matters as much as the route. Slide shaped blocks to matching doors, remove them, and use the newly opened space to solve the rest.\n\n## Clearing a block changes the board\n\nThe listing allows sliding blocks while obstacles constrain their paths. Reaching a matching door makes a block disappear. A useful move can therefore do more than finish one piece: it can open a corridor or free a larger area needed elsewhere.\n\nShape is explicitly part of the strategy. The developer encourages using each block’s outline to manage space, so the puzzle is not merely matching a colored square with a colored exit. A route that works for one piece may not accommodate another.\n\nThe description does not provide a complete movement diagram or specify whether rotation is available. It would be inaccurate to add a rotation rule just because shaped pieces are present. Similarly, it does not document the full range of later blockers, only that new ones are introduced as you progress.\n\n## Planning has a time boundary\n\nThe play guide says to plan before running out of time. That is a meaningful rule, especially because other parts of the description frame the game as a way to unwind. Relaxing presentation and a countdown can coexist, but readers choosing specifically for no timers should not overlook the latter.\n\nThis makes Color Block Jam most relevant to someone who likes spatial routing and can enjoy turning a plan into efficient actions. It is less suitable for a reader who wants unlimited time to examine every possible arrangement. The exact countdown lengths and recovery conditions are not established here.\n\n## Costs and comparisons\n\nThe saved US download is free. Ad frequency, paid recovery, booster prices, offline support, and no-spend progression are not documented in the supplied description. There are no saved customer review bodies for this entry to supply actual accounts of late-stage difficulty or interruptions.\n\nThe block-to-door premise overlaps with other sliding puzzles, but that does not justify importing their elevators, generators, or advertising systems. The supported differentiators here are shaped blocks, matching exits, changing obstacles, and an explicit time boundary.\n\nChoose on whether that combination sounds satisfying, not on a generic assumption that every colorful block puzzle uses the same rules.\n\n## Verdict\n\nColor Block Jam offers a clear space-clearing and routing concept, with block shapes adding useful structure. Consider it if a countdown sharpens that challenge; skip it if unlimited thinking time is nonnegotiable.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What is the goal in Color Block Jam?\n\nSlide colored blocks to their matching doors so they disappear and the board can be cleared.\n\n### Does Color Block Jam have a timer?\n\nThe supplied play guide explicitly refers to planning before running out of time.\n\n### Can blocks rotate?\n\nThe listing describes sliding and using shapes strategically, but does not establish a rotation feature.\n\n[View the US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/color-block-jam/id6504332779?uo=4).",
