    "bodyMarkdown": "# Royal Match: Match-3 Progress With a Castle to Restore\n\nRoyal Match gives each puzzle a destination outside the board: another part of King Robert's castle restored. Its listing is brief, but the connection between match-3 progress and unlocking new areas is clear. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## The board pays for the bigger picture\n\nThe developer describes clearing obstacles and combining power-ups to complete match-3 levels. Progress unlocks castle areas, including rooms, royal chambers, and gardens. Bonus levels offer coins, while chests and boosters provide additional rewards and tools.\n\nThe restoration theme is important because it frames success as more than another cleared stage. A completed board contributes to opening a new area. Players who enjoy a visible sense of advancement may find that structure more motivating than a standalone score chase.\n\nThe supplied text does not document every tile rule, obstacle, move allowance, or failure condition. It also does not establish how much control players have over the restoration design. Unlocking decorated spaces should not automatically be described as a freeform interior-design editor.\n\n## The castle is the hook, not proof of another game mode\n\nThe description centers on match-3 play. Someone expecting a different rescue or physics puzzle should use that stated core as the reliable starting point. King Robert's presence does not, by itself, document a particular rescue minigame or its availability.\n\nPower-ups and obstacles suggest that planning combinations matters, but their exact balance cannot be judged from a feature list. A booster can create an interesting tactical choice or simply ease a difficult stage; the saved text does not establish which role dominates later.\n\nThere are no usable player-review bodies in this collection. That prevents claims about players finding the difficulty fair, the rewards generous, or the castle progression repetitive. The store's rating aggregate is not a substitute for those missing accounts.\n\n## What the listing does not settle about cost\n\nThe recorded download price is free. The supplied description does not establish an ad schedule, a verified no-forced-ads policy, or the pricing and practical importance of paid assistance. None of those should be assumed from the game's reputation or its polished promotional language.\n\nIf your decision depends on uninterrupted play or a strict no-spending routine, those are questions for a direct inspection of the installed version and its offers rather than a conclusion this evidence can support.\n\n## Verdict\n\nRoyal Match is a clear thematic fit for people who like match-3 progression with a restoration backdrop. It is less clearly suited to players seeking a documented standalone logic challenge or extensive design freedom. The castle gives the levels context; the available material cannot establish the long-term economy or difficulty quality.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What type of puzzle is Royal Match?\nThe listing identifies match-3 levels with obstacles and combinable power-ups.\n\n### What do you restore?\nKing Robert's castle, with rooms, gardens, and other areas opening through progress.\n\n### Are rescue minigames verified here?\nNo. The supplied description establishes match-3 and restoration, not a specific rescue mode.\n\n### Is ad-free play confirmed?\nNo. This evidence does not establish advertising behavior.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/royal-match/id1482155847?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)",
