    "bodyMarkdown": "# My Sticker Room: Decorating Without Starting From a Blank Canvas\n\nMy Sticker Room offers a different kind of decorating fantasy: you do not have to decide where every object belongs. The listing describes placing stickers into their intended spots, making completion rather than open-ended design the central pleasure. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Peel, place, and finish the page\n\nEach level is presented as a sticker-book page. You peel up items, place them where they belong, and gradually fill a room or location. Animal characters and room decorations supply the theme, with a coffee shop among the described settings.\n\nThat gives the game a clear loop: identify the item, find its destination, and watch the scene become complete. It is closer to assembling a prepared illustration than designing a house from scratch. The developer explicitly frames freedom from choosing everything yourself as part of the appeal.\n\nFor players who enjoy finishing a scene but dislike deciding among many equally valid arrangements, that guidance could be an advantage. For someone who wants to express a personal interior-design style, it is an important limitation rather than a minor detail.\n\n## Cozy is the goal, not a verified effect\n\nThe description emphasizes simple mechanics, cute animals, and a calm atmosphere. Those are useful clues to the intended audience, but they do not prove that every level is easy or that every player finds the app soothing. No screenshots were visually inspected for this analysis, so specific claims about the actual room layouts or visual readability would go beyond the evidence.\n\nThe saved text also does not establish how accurately a sticker must be positioned, whether placement errors are penalized, or whether you can freely revisit completed scenes. Those details could make a meaningful difference on a smaller phone screen.\n\nNo customer-review bodies were available. The listing's suggestion that the game suits very short breaks is therefore not backed by measured session lengths or player reports about convenient stopping points.\n\n## Advertising and payment questions\n\nMy Sticker Room is listed as a free download. The supplied description does not establish ad frequency, paid scene packs, or any removal offer. A calm art direction does not automatically mean calm monetization, and no such conclusion is warranted here.\n\nIf interruption tolerance is central to your choice, inspect the installed flow before treating the game as a dependable quiet-time routine.\n\n## Verdict\n\nMy Sticker Room is a sensible prospect for people who enjoy guided picture completion and animal-themed décor. It is less suited to players seeking unrestricted furniture placement or demanding deduction. Its strongest documented quality is the lack of blank-canvas pressure: the intended result already exists, and your job is to bring it together.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can you design rooms freely?\nThe listing emphasizes placing stickers in the correct spots, not unrestricted room design.\n\n### What kinds of stickers are included?\nThe description mentions room décor, cats, bunnies, and other animal characters.\n\n### Are timers or penalties verified?\nNo. The saved text does not provide a complete rule set for those systems.\n\n### Is this confirmed to be a relaxing game?\nRelaxation is the developer's positioning; no playtest or usable customer sample establishes it here.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/my-sticker-room-decor-game/id6743738094?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)",
    "chartRank": 71
