    "bodyMarkdown": "# Yarn Fever! Unravel Puzzle: Soft Materials, Hard Storage Choices\n\nYarn Fever gives a constrained sorting puzzle the language of knitting and unraveling. The soft theme is inviting, but the actual decision described in the listing is a familiar strategic one: which item can you safely remove without exhausting your temporary space? This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Unravel in a useful order\n\nThe developer describes collecting colored threads from knitted objects and placing them into matching-color boxes. Threads may also occupy temporary slots. Fill too much of that space and progress becomes harder to manage.\n\nThat makes the order of collection important. Taking an available thread is not automatically helpful if its matching destination is unavailable and the buffer is nearly full. The satisfying idea is to turn a complicated object into organized colors while preserving room for the next move.\n\nThe saved text does not fully specify box capacities, access rules, or whether hidden threads are visible before removal. Those details should not be imported from screw-sorting games merely because the temporary-storage concept is similar.\n\n## More slots are a meaningful kind of assistance\n\nThe listing names tools including New Hole, Magic Box, and Broom. It also describes adding boxes and slots as customization. In a puzzle whose main constraint is space, additional storage can change the problem substantially; it is not merely a cosmetic option.\n\nThe description does not establish how these tools are earned or bought. It would be equally unsupported to declare that later levels demand payment or to promise that every tool is freely available. Their existence is documented; their balance is not.\n\nThe developer advertises increasingly complex levels, calming visuals, and ASMR-style appeal. No screenshots were visually inspected and no audio was heard for this analysis. Those sensory claims therefore remain promotional rather than an independent assessment of the actual presentation.\n\n## No player sample, incomplete cost information\n\nThere are no usable customer-review bodies in the saved evidence. That means there is no basis here for statements about player satisfaction, recurring bugs, or the frequency of ads.\n\nThe download is listed as free, but the supplied description does not document an ad-removal option or current assistance prices. A cozy craft theme does not settle the monetization question, and extra-slot language should be examined carefully before spending.\n\n## Verdict\n\nYarn Fever is a plausible fit for people who like color sorting, limited buffers, and the idea of dismantling a decorative object. It is less suitable if you want an unrestricted fidget toy or a verified low-pressure economy. The yarn is the theme; planning around temporary storage is the substantive puzzle.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What do you sort?\nColored threads collected from knitted objects, according to the listing.\n\n### Why do temporary slots matter?\nThey hold threads before matching placement, so using too much space can restrict progress.\n\n### Which tools are advertised?\nNew Hole, Magic Box, and Broom are named, alongside extra boxes and slots.\n\n### Are those tools free?\nThe saved description does not establish their prices or earning conditions.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/yarn-fever-unravel-puzzle/id6747875092?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)",
    "chartRank": 76
