    "bodyMarkdown": "# Tangle Master 3D: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nTangle Master 3D asks you to separate ropes in the right order while staying within a move limit. Its colorful knots are not simply an unrestricted toy you can rearrange indefinitely.\n\n## Order matters before the knot disappears\n\nThe description links sorting ropes, matching rope and pin colors, and undoing tangles. That suggests attention to both which strand moves and where it belongs. The full legal-move system is not documented, so it would be misleading to invent exact drag destinations or claim every pin behaves identically.\n\nThe developer presents two, three, and four ropes as escalating complexity. More strands mean more relationships to inspect, but the text does not establish a formal difficulty formula or a uniform sequence through every level.\n\nLimited moves are explicit. The description also says to untangle on time, though it does not clarify whether that phrase means a countdown on every board. A universal no-timer promise would be unsupported, as would a precise time limit.\n\nA promotional booster panel shows scissors and a lock-related tool. It confirms that assistance is prominent in the presentation, without establishing availability or a requirement to use it.\n\n## Boosters can bypass parts of a setup\n\nCutting a rope and exploding locks are named forms of help. Those tools alter the puzzle rather than merely highlighting a possible next move. Readers who like solving without destructive assists may value knowing the distinction.\n\nHowever, the description does not say how boosters are earned, whether they cost currency, or whether any stage requires one. Their existence alone is not evidence that the ordinary puzzle rules are impossible or that payment is mandatory.\n\nHundreds of levels, customization, and weekend tournaments are advertised. These provide a larger framework, but the exact tournament rules and unlock conditions remain unspecified. A competition label does not independently establish real-time multiplayer.\n\n## A visual sorting fit, with constraints to check\n\nConsider Tangle Master if following overlapping strands and planning their release sounds appealing. Skip it if you want a purely verbal riddle or a sandbox with no failure budget. The listing’s brain-training language does not demonstrate an increase in intelligence or a measured cognitive benefit.\n\nThe US download is free. There are no customer review bodies in this sample, so no player consensus about frustration, ad frequency, or control comfort can be drawn. Purchases, offline access, and paid removal are also not established by the supplied description.\n\nThe most useful expectation is a constrained untangling problem with color cues and optional forms of assistance. The exact pressure and generosity of those systems remain open.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTangle Master 3D is relevant to readers who enjoy visual strand tracing under a move budget. Its relaxing presentation should not be mistaken for proof of unlimited mistakes or an absence of time pressure.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Are moves limited?\n\nYes. The description explicitly states a limited number of moves to complete a level.\n\n### What boosters are named?\n\nThe listing mentions cutting a rope and exploding locks.\n\n### Does every level have a timer?\n\nThe phrase on time appears, but the description does not establish a countdown on every level.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tangle-master-3d/id1512799121?uo=4)."
