    "bodyMarkdown": "# Wood Nuts & Bolts Puzzle: Undo the Structure, Not the Colors\n\nWood Nuts & Bolts Puzzle uses fasteners as obstacles in a dismantling problem. Its premise is different from stacking colored nuts: you rearrange bolts so wooden plates can be removed. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Think about what each fastener is holding\n\nThe listing describes twists, turns, and strategic moves through wooden puzzles, with bolts rearranged to clear plates. The relevant question is therefore structural: which change allows another part of the arrangement to come free?\n\nA seemingly helpful removal may alter what can be done next. The appeal is considering the order of operations rather than just recognizing matching colors. That is a general reading of the mechanic, not evidence of a specific physics behavior or level solution.\n\nThe supplied text does not establish spare-hole counts, color-coded collection boxes, or rules for a fastener dropping into a tray. Those features belong to some neighboring screw puzzles, but they should not be silently added here.\n\n## Multiple solutions, limited assistance\n\nThe developer advertises more than 300 levels, varying difficulty, and several ways to solve a puzzle. A limited hint system offers help with difficult situations.\n\nMultiple solutions could suit players who enjoy experimenting instead of searching for one prescribed sequence. However, the statement does not prove that every level has several equally valid paths, or that the app explains why a failed attempt was wrong.\n\nLimited hints are also a meaningful detail. They suggest that help is a resource, but the supplied evidence does not state how it is replenished or whether it costs money or a video. It would be premature to call the assistance generous or restrictive without those terms.\n\nSkins and global competition are advertised as extras. They change presentation or provide a score-related goal, but the description does not establish that they change the dismantling rules.\n\n## Free access and unanswered practical questions\n\nThe metadata records a free download. No customer-review bodies are available, so there is no basis for statements about player frustration, ad frequency, satisfying physics, or later-level fairness.\n\nThe evidence also does not independently verify offline operation, stability, or the absence of time pressure. Promotional language about relaxing or sharpening skills does not settle those practical questions.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWood Nuts & Bolts Puzzle looks most suitable for players who enjoy dependency chains and carefully taking an arrangement apart. It is less suitable as a recommendation for someone specifically seeking a color-sorting screw game. The plate-and-bolt concept is distinctive enough to identify the audience, but assistance costs and actual handling remain untested.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Are you sorting nuts by color?\nThe listing describes rearranging bolts to remove wooden plates instead.\n\n### Are hints unlimited?\nNo. The developer explicitly describes a limited hint system.\n\n### Is only one solution allowed?\nMultiple solutions are advertised, though not independently verified for every puzzle.\n\n### Are color-coded screw boxes confirmed?\nNo. That mechanic is not established in the supplied description.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/wood-nuts-bolts-puzzle/id6472426288?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
