    "bodyMarkdown": "# Hexa Sort: Stack Satisfaction Meets a Busy Progression Layer\n\nHexa Sort combines sorting with the anticipation of a stack finally lining up. Reviewers in the sample often recognize that appeal, even when they dislike the extra cards, side activities, or interruptions surrounding it. This source-based review combines the US App Store listing with player reports; it is not a hands-on playtest.\n\n## Sorting and merging share the board\n\nThe developer describes shuffling and arranging hexagonal stacks, matching colors, and merging toward collection goals. Boosters help with harder stages, while sound and animations are promoted as part of the sensory appeal.\n\nThe concept is more than a conventional row-clearing block puzzle. You are considering where a stack belongs and how its colors interact with the arrangement already present. The supplied description does not fully specify every automatic transfer rule, so exact chain reactions should not be promised from the listing alone.\n\nThat leaves the central audience distinction clear: this is for players who enjoy organizing a developing board, not necessarily those seeking a fixed deduction puzzle with one cleanly stated answer.\n\n## Satisfaction is not the only recurring theme\n\nThe review sample contains 50 US App Store reviews dated 2026-08-24 through 2026-11-06 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 6.2.31, 6.2.50, 6.2.61, 6.2.62, 6.3.00, 6.3.11, 6.3.20, 6.3.30, 6.3.41, 6.3.50, 6.3.60, 6.4.00, 6.4.11; the listing records version 6.4.20. Apple's most-recent RSS sample is capped at 50 and self-selected, not representative of all players or a live consensus. These are player reports, not independently verified findings.\n\nSome reviewers call the game fun or satisfying. One detailed account likes the core puzzle but dislikes card-related animations; another finds side activities distracting. These are useful distinctions because a player can appreciate the mechanic without wanting all of its progression systems.\n\nSeveral accounts describe crashes, lost progress, or freezing. They do not provide a measured stability rate, and the sample versions differ from the listing version. They do identify an issue to watch for before attaching much value to a long streak or resource balance.\n\nA separate set of reviewers says offline use no longer works as expected. That is a reported change, not an independently verified current connection requirement.\n\n## Sound, ads, and the meaning of removal\n\nSome comments describe audio from advertisements despite muted game settings or interruptions during play. The concern is not simply the existence of ads but their interference with a session intended to feel calming.\n\nOther players question what paid removal actually covers. The evidence does not establish a current price or a uniform entitlement, so no blanket removal promise is warranted. A reviewer who likes the game but finds coins expensive also cannot establish an objective cost of completing every stage.\n\n## Verdict\n\nHexa Sort may fit players attracted to color organization and stack-building satisfaction. It is less clearly suited to someone who requires a minimal presentation, dependable offline access, or a confirmed quiet-audio setup. The sample supports the core concept's appeal while cautioning against treating its relaxing branding as a guarantee about the whole session.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is Hexa Sort a line-clearing block game?\nIts listing emphasizes arranging hexagonal stacks, color matching, and merging instead.\n\n### Are all transfer rules documented?\nNo. The supplied description leaves some automatic interactions unspecified.\n\n### Is offline play independently verified?\nNo. Several reviewers report a change, but disconnected behavior was not tested.\n\n### Does muted game audio guarantee silent ads?\nNo. Some sampled accounts specifically report unwanted ad sound.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/hexa-sort/id6463127238?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
