    "bodyMarkdown": "# ColorPlanet Paint by Number: Completion Without a Blank Canvas\n\nColorPlanet Paint by Number is aimed at someone who wants to finish a picture without first designing it. The pleasure it promises is gradual completion, not the uncertainty of choosing every line and color yourself. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Match the number, fill the region\n\nThe developer describes numbered areas paired with palette colors. Tapping the matching regions develops a prepared picture. Tips can help with difficult-to-find areas, and progress saving supports returning to an unfinished image.\n\nThat is a guided activity rather than an unrestricted art tool. The decisions revolve around what to color and which remaining regions to locate, not how to construct the subject from scratch. Someone seeking drawing lessons or free brushwork should not confuse the paint-by-number label with those features.\n\nThe description does not fully specify zoom controls, region size, or the way unfinished areas are highlighted. Those practical details can determine whether a dense image feels absorbing or tiring, especially on a small screen.\n\n## A category-led library\n\nThe listing advertises more than 3,000 pictures, multiple categories, and daily additions. The breadth is relevant if choosing an image is part of the enjoyment: a player may want a simple subject one day and something more detailed the next.\n\nThe count remains a developer claim, not an independently checked inventory or a guarantee that every picture is accessible for free. Daily updates also do not establish a particular notification schedule or a required daily task.\n\nNo screenshot was visually inspected here, so there is no independent assessment of the art style or palette. The evidence supports describing a catalog of guided pictures, not declaring them beautiful or easy to see.\n\n## Help, saving, and access remain partly unspecified\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available for this app in the supplied collection. It is therefore not possible to report whether players find tips useful, progress dependable, or new content varied.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. The text does not establish whether tips require ads or purchases, how often ads appear, or whether the catalog works offline. It would be equally unsupported to promise generosity or accuse the game of gating every useful feature.\n\nRelaxation is the intended appeal, not a clinically established outcome. The meaningful fit question is whether methodically filling prescribed areas sounds enjoyable to you.\n\n## Verdict\n\nColorPlanet Paint by Number is a plausible choice for players who like visible progress and a prepared image to work toward. It is less suited to someone looking for open-ended painting or verified accessibility controls. The central activity is clear; the conditions around hints, content access, and uninterrupted use remain undocumented.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is this free-form painting?\nNo. The main activity matches numbered areas to prescribed colors.\n\n### Can you return to an unfinished picture?\nProgress saving is advertised, though not independently tested.\n\n### Are tips available?\nYes. Their cost and replenishment conditions are not established here.\n\n### Is every advertised picture confirmed free?\nNo. A library count does not establish complete access terms.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/colorplanet-paint-by-number/id1492055041?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
