    "bodyMarkdown": "# Shape Escape: Block Puzzle: A Familiar Grid With Specific VIP Terms\n\nShape Escape: Block Puzzle describes a placement-and-line-clearing game beneath its escape-themed name. The most unusually specific part of its listing is not the escape rule, but the range of auto-renewing VIP durations. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Fit the shape and protect the remaining space\n\nThe developer describes dragging blocks onto a board, clearing completed lines, and managing limited room. No time limit is advertised, giving the concept a deliberate rather than reflex-driven pace.\n\nThe practical challenge is choosing placements that serve a line without leaving the rest of the grid awkwardly fragmented. A block that fits now may create a gap that is hard to use later. That is a general consequence of the stated premise, not evidence about the app's actual piece sequence.\n\nThe supplied text does not fully define an escape objective separate from line clearing. It also does not establish grid dimensions or rotation rules. The title should not be turned into an invented campaign of freeing a particular shape through an exit.\n\n## Quiet timing is not the same as quiet access\n\nOffline play and no time limit are developer claims. They do not independently establish that every mode works disconnected, that every session saves reliably, or that advertisements never appear.\n\nThere are no usable customer-review bodies here. Consequently, there is no evidence-based player account of difficulty, controls, or value. A clean description of a rule is not a substitute for an assessment of how well that rule is implemented.\n\nThe game may interest players who enjoy slowly improving spatial placements. It is less clearly suited to someone looking for a specifically documented escape mechanic rather than score-oriented line clearing.\n\n## The listed subscription durations deserve attention\n\nThe supplied description lists VIP at $4.99 weekly, $4.99 monthly, $19.99 for six months, and $29.99 yearly. Those are the source's stated alternatives, not a verified current checkout. Weekly and monthly are different billing periods even when the written amount happens to match.\n\nThe advertised benefits include no ads and spins. The plans auto-renew, so the initial download price is not the same as the cost of retaining a chosen subscription. No claim is made here about which plan is currently offered to a particular account.\n\n## Verdict\n\nShape Escape is a plausible fit for players who want untimed block placement and are comfortable checking access terms themselves. It is a weaker choice based solely on the escape name. The line-clearing loop is recognizable; the exact extra objective and current VIP availability remain unverified.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is a literal escape route documented?\nThe supplied text does not fully define one beyond fitting blocks and clearing lines.\n\n### Is the game advertised as untimed?\nYes. No time limit is a developer claim.\n\n### Are weekly and monthly VIP the same duration?\nNo. They are separate billing periods despite matching listed dollar amounts.\n\n### Does VIP automatically renew?\nThe description identifies the plans as auto-renewing subscriptions.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/shape-escape-block-puzzle/id6743091090?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
