    "bodyMarkdown": "# Found It!: Search the Whole Map, Not Just the First View\n\nFound It! presents hidden-object searching as an exploration task. The listing describes interactive maps that you pan and zoom through, rather than a single picture kept entirely on screen. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Move the view as well as your attention\n\nThe developer describes finding listed objects, completing quests, and opening further locations. Zoom and map movement support searching beyond the initial view, while hints offer assistance when a target remains elusive.\n\nThat creates a practical memory task within the search. You need to distinguish an area that has already been inspected from one that has not, and an overview may serve a different purpose from a close-up.\n\nThe supplied description does not establish exact gesture controls, maximum magnification, or how target lists change between quests. It also does not fully document whether a target can be moved or interacted with before collection. Those details should not be added because the map is called interactive.\n\n## A broad scene can be attractive or demanding\n\nThe developer advertises several kinds of locations and increasing challenge. A large scene may appeal to someone who enjoys leisurely visual discovery. It may be less comfortable for someone who wants a bounded page with every target and clue visible at once.\n\nThose are potential tradeoffs, not player feedback. No usable customer-review bodies are available here, and no screenshot was visually inspected. Specific hidden-object positions or visual jokes are therefore outside the evidence.\n\nThe advertised hint system is relevant but incomplete as a comparison point. A hint may reduce a frustrating search, yet its usefulness depends on what it reveals and how often it can be used. Neither the precise behavior nor the replenishment terms are fully established.\n\n## Access conditions remain unknown\n\nThe US metadata lists a free download. The supplied text does not establish advertising frequency, paid assistance, an ad-removal offer, or offline access. There is no basis for declaring either an aggressive economy or an unrestricted one.\n\nLikewise, the broad challenge language does not establish a timer or mistake penalty. Completing quests to unlock content is documented; all the constraints governing that progression are not.\n\n## Verdict\n\nFound It! is most relevant to players who enjoy exploring a map while searching for recognizable objects. It is less clearly suited to someone who requires a fully visible workspace or verified accessibility options. The pan-and-zoom format and quest progression are concrete attractions, while practical comfort and assistance terms remain untested.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can you move around the search area?\nYes. Panning and zooming are described in the listing.\n\n### What opens new locations?\nThe description links finding objects and completing quests with unlocking further maps.\n\n### Are hints advertised?\nYes, though their precise effects and cost are not fully established.\n\n### Is the game confirmed to have no time pressure?\nNo complete timer or penalty rules are documented in the supplied text.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/found-it-hidden-object-game/id1643547847?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
