    "bodyMarkdown": "# Ball Sort Puzzle - Color Game: Four Slots Make Every Move Count\n\nBall Sort Puzzle - Color Game documents a useful constraint: each bottle holds four balls. That gives its color-grouping task a definite capacity problem rather than an unspecified sorting surface. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Move the top ball, preserve a destination\n\nThe listing describes selecting a bottle and transferring its top ball. The receiving bottle needs room, and the move follows a same-color rule. The goal is to gather each color into a single bottle.\n\nFour slots make temporary storage valuable. Exposing a buried ball can require moving other colors first, and those temporary moves need somewhere legal to go. Completing one color too eagerly may use a bottle you would otherwise have kept as working space.\n\nThat is a general planning implication, not a solution for a specific level. The supplied text does not fully explain all empty-bottle exceptions or how many bottles appear in each puzzle, so those rules should not be invented.\n\n## Recovery tools are explicitly part of the pitch\n\nUndo, adding a bottle, and restarting are advertised. These serve different purposes: undo can reverse a decision, an extra bottle changes available space, and restart lets you reconsider the sequence from the beginning.\n\nTheir presence may suit someone who likes experimenting rather than protecting a perfect first attempt. However, the listing does not establish whether adding a bottle is unlimited, earned, video-gated, or paid. A tool existing is not the same as having unrestricted free access to it.\n\nThe description also advertises no timer and no penalties. Those claims concern the intended pace and consequence structure, not an independently verified promise that every feature has no limits.\n\n## Free and offline are separate questions\n\nThe metadata records a free download, and offline use is promoted. No customer-review bodies are available here to assess how well the recovery tools work or whether players find the later puzzles varied.\n\nAdvertising frequency, removal terms, and current assistance prices remain undocumented. No disconnected session or stability test was performed. The combination of free download and offline marketing should not automatically become a no-forced-ads label.\n\nThe relevant appeal is still clear: visible colors, limited top-piece access, and a defined capacity encourage planning several moves ahead.\n\n## Verdict\n\nThis Ball Sort game looks most suitable for players who want a four-slot sorting puzzle with advertised recovery options. It is less conclusive for someone who needs unlimited free assistance or verified quiet offline use. Its capacity rule and distinction between undo, restart, and extra space are the most useful documented details.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### How many balls fit in a bottle?\nThe listing specifies four.\n\n### Which ball can move?\nThe top ball, subject to matching-color and available-space rules.\n\n### Is adding a bottle advertised?\nYes, but its availability and cost are not fully established.\n\n### Does no penalty mean every assist is free?\nNo. That conclusion is not supported by the supplied description.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/ball-sort-puzzle-color-game/id1625097467?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
