    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Oasis: Calm Puzzle Game: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2026-10-20–2026-11-09 (Asia/Shanghai), covering version 1.14.5. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nWord Oasis: Calm Puzzle Game connects anagram solving to a growing landscape. Swipe letters into answers, collect milestone illustrations, and use progress to develop a personal oasis.\n\n## Growth is the surrounding reward\n\nThe developer describes words planting seeds and growing trees, making visible progress part of the reason to keep solving. The official image shows answer slots and a circular letter pool over an autumn landscape, clarifying the word-building activity beneath that theme.\n\nUnlimited refreshes, no timers, no penalties, and no-Wi-Fi play are advertised. These are product claims, not hands-on findings. The description does not fully explain the oasis-building controls or whether every decorative choice is freely placed.\n\n## Support centers on words and presentation\n\nOne reviewer specifically enjoys finding both correct answers and bonus words. Another likes how quickly the solving moves, and a separate account praises soothing sound. Those are useful reasons to consider it without treating personal enjoyment as evidence of improved memory.\n\nA contrasting reviewer says there are no directions and describes the game as guessing. That is an individual instruction concern, not proof that no tutorial exists in every installation. The limited sample also contains many brief endorsements that cannot support detailed claims about later-level design.\n\nThe listing’s eye-protection and brain-training language remains marketing. Neither a blue interface nor a player’s health testimonial establishes a clinical benefit or treatment effect.\n\n## Free does not mean universally ad-free\n\nOne reviewer reports fewer distractions under a no-ads title. Others describe recurring or unclosable ads. Two purchasers say advertising continued after payment, including one who identifies a yearly removal purchase.\n\nThe written description’s claim of being totally free therefore should not be expanded into a verified absence of paid offers. Nor can the mixed reports establish what each purchase was intended to remove. All sampled entries list version 1.14.5, so version differences alone do not explain the disagreement.\n\nThe US download is free. Current removal prices, subscription terms, and actual offline coverage have not been independently checked.\n\nConsider Word Oasis if finding words and seeing a landscape grow are both appealing. Readers choosing specifically for a confirmed ad-free routine should inspect the actual offer and interruption pattern first rather than relying on the calm branding.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Oasis has specific support for its word discoveries and presentation. Its best-supported caution is the gap between a free, calm pitch and conflicting advertising experiences, including purchaser complaints.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is Word Oasis a word-search grid?\n\nThe advertised action is connecting letters, and the official image shows a circular letter pool with answer slots.\n\n### Are there timers?\n\nThe developer explicitly advertises no timers and no penalties; this has not been playtested.\n\n### Does paying guarantee no ads?\n\nTwo reviewers report ads after payment. Current offer scope and entitlement behavior remain unverified.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-oasis-calm-puzzle-game/id6745003362?uo=4)."
