    "bodyMarkdown": "# Hoop Stack: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2021-07-14–2026-08-10 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 0.9.0–0.9.6. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nHoop Stack turns color sorting into a peg-and-ring arrangement. Move through mixed stacks toward an organized result, with the next useful move depending on the hoops already above and below one another.\n\n## A simple concept with an incomplete rule sheet\n\nThe description promises sorting colorful hoops and predicting moves. The official image shows several stacks and an empty peg, making temporary space part of the visible setup. It does not establish every transfer restriction or a universal peg capacity.\n\nOne reviewer describes the challenge as just right, while another wants harder stages and more hoop designs. A different long-term account uses it mainly to keep their hands occupied. Those are different expectations for the same organizing loop.\n\nThe sample stretches from July 2021 to August 2026. It is historical evidence, not recent feedback from a single release cycle. Old control requests should not be presented as proof that current functionality remains absent.\n\n## Novelty and solvability are separate questions\n\nSome reviewers say patterns repeat after extended play. Another asks for whole-stack lifting and easier transfer behavior. That request identifies a desired convenience, not a verified statement that a present-day version cannot move a group.\n\nA later reviewer describes reaching a position with no legal moves and says undo reset the whole stage. This supports a frustration report, not proof that the original puzzle had no solution. A blocked position can result from earlier choices, and no board reconstruction was performed here.\n\nAn older colorblind reviewer specifically struggles to distinguish green shades. That is more useful than assuming bright colors are readable for everyone, although current accessibility settings have not been checked.\n\n## The payment reports need present-day confirmation\n\nSeveral purchasers report advertising after a no-ads payment. Others describe frequent between-level interruptions, while an older positive account appreciates the lack of mid-level ads. Those accounts do not establish one current schedule or offer scope.\n\nThe US download is free. Actual removal prices, offline functionality, and tool availability remain unverified. Freeze and loading complaints also appear, without device-level reproduction.\n\nConsider Hoop Stack if arranging colors is enjoyable independently of a continually novel campaign. Readers who need strong accessibility support, dependable undo, or confirmed ad removal should not treat those qualities as established by the simple presentation.\n\n## Verdict\n\nHoop Stack has supporters of its straightforward sorting, but its broad historical sample raises separate concerns about repetition, color distinction, and commercial interruptions. Current rules and access terms deserve checking.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can similar green hoops be hard to distinguish?\n\nOne historical reviewer with color-vision difficulties specifically reports trouble with green shades. Current alternative cues were not assessed.\n\n### Does a blocked board prove an impossible puzzle?\n\nNo. One reviewer reports no legal moves, but the starting board and preceding choices were not independently reconstructed.\n\n### Is ad removal confirmed?\n\nSeveral purchasers report remaining ads. The present offer and entitlement coverage are not verified.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/hoop-stack/id1494502529?uo=4)."
