    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Guess - Word Games: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nWord Guess - Word Games gives you six attempts to identify a mystery word. Each submitted guess becomes information for the next one through a three-color feedback system.\n\n## Read the color as a constraint\n\nGray means the letter is absent. Orange means the letter belongs in the answer but not in that position. Green marks a correct letter in the correct place. That turns an unsuccessful guess into a set of restrictions rather than simply a lost turn.\n\nA useful next guess must account for what is already known while exploring what remains uncertain. That is the central deduction appeal, not a promise that one opening word will always solve the puzzle.\n\nThe official image shows five-letter guesses, a matching on-screen keyboard, and colored feedback across several rows. It demonstrates a five-letter example, but the brief written description does not establish that every available mode always uses that length.\n\n## Six tries create a defined budget\n\nA limit of six attempts distinguishes this from an unrestricted anagram search. Each submission uses part of that budget, so there is a trade-off between testing possibilities and committing to a likely answer.\n\nThe description does not explain duplicate-letter handling, acceptable guess dictionaries, or whether invalid words consume a turn. Those details matter considerably in a feedback puzzle and should not be imported automatically from another familiar word game.\n\nNor does the listing establish a daily-only schedule, unlimited puzzle access, answer sharing, or a hard mode. A recognizable format is not proof of every feature associated with it elsewhere.\n\n## A compact concept for deduction fans\n\nConsider Word Guess if you enjoy eliminating letters and positions through evidence. It is less suitable if you mainly want crossword clues, visible scrambled letters, or a story reward after each board.\n\nThe color system is also a practical selection issue. The official image uses color prominently, but the supplied description does not identify an alternative symbol mode or color-vision settings. Their absence from this evidence is not proof that none exist; it is a reason to check if they matter to you.\n\nThe US download is free. Advertising, purchases, offline support, statistics, and retry conditions are not established. There are no customer review bodies in this sample to support claims about word-list quality or unobtrusive play.\n\nChoose on the clearly documented six-guess deduction loop, not assumptions about a complete feature match with another app.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Guess communicates its core feedback rules clearly. It is a concept fit for constrained word deduction, while dictionary details, repeated letters, and access conditions remain important unanswered questions.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### How many guesses do you get?\n\nThe listing specifies six attempts to identify the mystery word.\n\n### What does orange mean?\n\nThe letter is in the answer but in the wrong position.\n\n### How are repeated letters handled?\n\nThe supplied description does not document duplicate-letter feedback rules.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-guess-word-games/id1603978681?uo=4)."
