    "bodyMarkdown": "# Wood Screw: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2026-03-07–2026-11-06 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 2.6, 3.0. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nWood Screw asks you to release a wooden construction by removing fasteners in a useful order. Its strongest selection issue is a direct conflict: the description promises no time limit, while several reviewers report timers.\n\n## Removal changes the construction\n\nThe listing describes unscrewing and repositioning pins so wooden elements can drop away. The official image shows a layered watch-shaped assembly held by screws, with spare holes around it. That makes access and removal order visible as the core problem.\n\nA piece may remain supported or obstruct a useful location until other fasteners move. The description does not document every physical interaction, temporary-storage rule, or tool, so a complete solution method would be speculative.\n\nSeveral reviewers still call the game fun or challenging despite criticizing its surrounding systems. This is not evidence that the puzzle concept lacks appeal; it is evidence that enjoying it does not erase access problems.\n\n## No-timer marketing is not a verified finding\n\nOne positive May account specifically praises playing without a timer. Other accounts, including later version-3.0 entries, say time limits appear as early as level five. A March reviewer even revisits the question and says the timer remains.\n\nThese differences should remain explicit. The evidence does not establish whether modes, offers, or another factor explain them. It does establish that recommending the whole app as reliably untimed would ignore substantial contrary reports.\n\n## Watching can fail to unlock the intended tool\n\nDetailed reviews repeatedly describe videos that do not award an extra hole, undo, screwdriver, or other promised assistance. The concern is delivery, not merely disliking ads: a player accepts an interruption and still cannot make the desired move.\n\nPurchasers also report continuing videos or broken reward flows after an ad-related offer. That does not establish what every paid package covers. Current prices and entitlements are unverified; the US download is free.\n\nA September reviewer explicitly says Daily Rewards were fixed. That improvement should not be omitted, but it does not resolve separate reports about video-earned tools. An achievement overlay that cannot be cleared is another individual interface complaint, not a reproduced defect.\n\nConsider Wood Screw for mechanical sequencing only with caution about the documented timer conflict and reward-delivery reports. Offline support and current stability have not been tested.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWood Screw has a recognizable fastener-order puzzle, but its untimed promise is contradicted by multiple sampled accounts. Broken optional-reward reports are especially relevant when assistance is needed to continue.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is Wood Screw definitely untimed?\n\nNo. The description says no time limit, but several reviewers report timers, while one account reports untimed play.\n\n### Do reward ads reliably grant tools?\n\nMultiple reviewers say promised tools or extra holes were not delivered. The behavior has not been independently reproduced.\n\n### Were Daily Rewards fixed?\n\nOne September reviewer explicitly reports a fix to Daily Rewards; that is separate from video-tool complaints.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/wood-screw/id6474293450?uo=4)."
