    "bodyMarkdown": "# Daily Themed Crossword Puzzles: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nDaily Themed Crossword Puzzles offers a clue-led alternative to swiping letters into words. Read a prompt, enter an answer into a crossing grid, and use the day’s theme as context.\n\n## Topics provide the daily frame\n\nThe description names movies, sports, technology, games, history, and architecture among its subjects. A different theme each day of the week is intended to vary the knowledge involved, rather than simply changing the background behind an anagram pool.\n\nThe official image shows a clue for Dwayne Johnson beneath a small crossword and a keyboard. It is a concrete example of general-knowledge answer entry. It does not establish the difficulty or clue quality of the whole catalog.\n\nCrossing answers can provide additional letters when a clue is unfamiliar. That is the format’s natural attraction for someone who enjoys combining vocabulary with trivia. The description does not establish automatic error marking, alternate spellings, or how proper names are checked.\n\n## A daily puzzle and an archive are different access layers\n\nA new puzzle every day and daily rewards are advertised. Hints are offered for obscure words, but the text does not fully specify what each hint reveals or the ordinary free allowance.\n\nVIP adds five archived puzzles daily, unlimited Mini Archive access, and a daily coin bonus. That is not the same as an explicit promise of unlimited access to the entire main archive. Readers who want to work through a large backlog should inspect that distinction.\n\nThe description also promises no ads for VIP. This is a developer benefit claim, not a tested finding about actual commercial behavior. A free download does not establish that every clue collection or archived date is open.\n\n## The quoted currency is not a US price\n\nThe supplied listing gives membership amounts in Singapore-dollar notation, despite this being the US app record. Those figures should not be silently relabeled as US dollars or converted into a purported current checkout offer.\n\nMembership is described as automatically renewing, with cancellation required before the stated renewal cutoff. The actual US price, trial eligibility, and present benefit coverage remain unverified.\n\nThere are no customer review bodies in this sample. Offline support, stability, and player views about fairness or cultural breadth are not established. Claims of rapid vocabulary improvement remain marketing, not measured educational results.\n\nConsider Daily Themed Crossword if clues and rotating topics are the activity you want. It is less suitable if you are seeking letter-bank word construction or unrestricted archive access without checking membership terms.\n\n## Verdict\n\nDaily Themed Crossword has a clear daily-clue proposition and specifically limited archive benefits. Confirm the actual US subscription offer rather than treating the description’s foreign-currency amounts as a valid local quote.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is it a letter-swiping game?\n\nThe official image shows clue-based crossword entry with a keyboard and crossing grid.\n\n### Does VIP unlock the entire main archive without limits?\n\nThe listed benefit is five archived puzzles daily, plus unlimited Mini Archive access—not an explicit unlimited main-archive promise.\n\n### What is the US membership price?\n\nIt is unresolved. The supplied description quotes Singapore-dollar notation rather than a verified US checkout price.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/daily-themed-crossword-puzzles/id1197354394?uo=4)."
