    "bodyMarkdown": "# Triple Match 3D: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nTriple Match 3D combines visual searching with a deadline. Find three identical items, clear the required objects, and reach the level’s goal before its timer expires.\n\n## Identify sets in a busy collection\n\nThe instructions say to tap three identical tiles and continue matching until the board is cleared. They also refer to goals set at the start of a level. The safest reading is to check each level’s stated objective rather than assume every mission uses an identical target list.\n\nThis is not a promise of classic mahjong solitaire rules. The description addresses mahjong fans, but matching triples of objects is a different premise from removing exposed tile pairs.\n\nThe inspected first official image shows the Triple Match logo and a loaded toy-like vehicle in a colorful landscape. It is promotional artwork, not a gameplay board from which storage slots, target counts, or object-selection gestures can be independently confirmed.\n\n## Relaxed language does not remove the clock\n\nThe description repeatedly calls the game relaxing, but explicitly states that every level has a timer and requires quick movement. That is the more useful detail for someone deciding whether the format suits them.\n\nSearching for a third copy while also tracking remaining goals can create a different demand from leisurely hidden-object browsing. The presence of a timer does not establish its duration, whether it can be paused, or the consequences of each incorrect selection.\n\nReaders who need an untimed experience should not interpret the pastel imagery as a no-pressure guarantee. No alternative no-clock mode is established in the supplied text.\n\n## Assistance changes the search field\n\nBoosters are advertised for difficult levels, and Shuffle rearranges the items. Rearranging can make a crowded collection look different, but the listing does not specify booster allowances, unlock conditions, or whether their supply is free.\n\nIt also does not document holding capacity or loss through collecting unmatched objects. Those are common questions for this family, not rules that can safely be borrowed from another triple-matching app.\n\nThe US download is free, and offline play without Wi-Fi is advertised. Current advertising, purchases, removal offers, and full offline feature coverage remain untested.\n\nThe developer specifically warns that its ads do not necessarily show actual gameplay. There are no customer review bodies in this sample to compare marketing with experience. Consider Triple Match for timed three-of-a-kind object searching, not because an external advertisement suggests a different puzzle.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTriple Match 3D has a concrete timed-triples premise with shuffle and boosters. Its explicit timer and marketing disclaimer are more decision-useful than broad relaxation language, particularly for readers avoiding pressured searches.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### How many identical items make a match?\n\nThe instructions specify three identical items.\n\n### Is it untimed?\n\nNo. The description explicitly says each level has a timer; no alternate untimed mode is established.\n\n### Do its ads necessarily show gameplay?\n\nNo. The developer expressly says Triple Match 3D ads do not necessarily show actual gameplay.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/triple-match-3d/id1607122287?uo=4)."
