    "bodyMarkdown": "# Bus Jam: Sort the Passengers, Then Check the Waiting Space\n\nBus Jam is primarily about sending passengers to matching buses, not merely sliding vehicles out of a parking lot. The sample shows why a clear color relationship and reliable completion matter to that simple premise. This source-based review combines the US App Store listing with player reports; it is not a hands-on playtest.\n\n## Keep the passenger flow useful\n\nThe developer describes organizing passengers, matching them to buses, clearing a path, and using powerups across progressively harder stages. The description does not fully specify waiting-space capacity or all boarding restrictions.\n\nA player reports being able to use only six of seven apparent waiting positions. That is an account of perceived capacity, not a verified rule to prescribe for every version.\n\nThe general challenge is sequencing. Moving someone out of the way can open access, but that person also needs a useful destination. A move can solve a local obstruction while complicating the larger flow.\n\n## Enjoyment often survives the complaint\n\nReviewers in this sample contributed 50 US App Store reviews dated 2025-05-21 through 2026-10-25 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 53.0.0, 53.0.1, 54.0.0, 54.0.1, 55.0.0, 56.0.0, 56.0.1, 57.0.0, 57.0.1, 58.0.0, 59.0.0, 59.0.1, 60.0.0, 61.0.0, 62.1.0, 62.10.1000, 62.6.1, 62.6.3, 67.0.1, 73.0.0, 75.0.0, 81.0.1, 81.0.2, 81.0.4, 81.0.6, 82.0.0, 82.1.1, 82.1.2, 82.3.1, 82.3.8, 82.8.1, 82.8.3, 82.9.1, 83.3.3, 83.3.4; the listing records version 82.9.3. Apple's most-recent RSS sample is capped at 50 and self-selected, not representative of all players or a live consensus. These are player reports, not independently verified findings.\n\nPositive reviewers enjoy the mix of moves, planning, and a relatively relaxed rhythm. One calls it cute and fun while criticizing colors that look too similar.\n\nMany critical accounts still like the game but report crashing after a completed stage and having to replay it. Another reviewer updates their complaint to say a release fixed the problem. These histories do not establish current stability, especially across a window reaching into 2025.\n\nSeveral players feel later levels depend on boosters or offer insufficient coins. That does not independently prove every stage is impossible without payment, but it identifies a progression concern distinct from understanding the sorting rules.\n\n## Ads and internal flourishes are different interruptions\n\nA historical account describes lighter, shorter ads than some competitors, while another complains that videos consume an awarded unlimited-life period. Current intervals and durations were not independently measured.\n\nA separate reviewer wants fewer win-streak and collection prompts. Those are internal presentation systems, not necessarily third-party advertisements.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. Historical removal-price comments do not establish a current universal offer, and no offline capability is independently verified.\n\n## Verdict\n\nBus Jam may suit players who enjoy planning a sequence of passenger moves toward matching destinations. It is a more cautious choice for someone who needs strongly differentiated colors or dependable long-session progress. The sample supports the core appeal while raising practical concerns about completion, assistance, and the screens surrounding it.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is this mainly vehicle unblocking?\nThe listing emphasizes sorting passengers onto their matching buses.\n\n### Is the waiting capacity confirmed?\nNo. A player discusses apparent slots, but the complete rule is not documented.\n\n### Are booster purchases proven mandatory?\nNo. Difficulty complaints are not a universal payment requirement.\n\n### Are crashes confirmed to persist today?\nNo. Reports span versions, including one account of a fix.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/bus-jam/id6450176534?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
