    "bodyMarkdown": "# Woody Block Puzzle: A Ten-by-Ten Run With a Story Alternative\n\nWoody Block Puzzle combines a familiar long-run grid challenge with a newer story-oriented alternative. Its listing is specific about the ten-by-ten board, making the core spatial task easier to compare than the broader relaxation claims. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Clear lines without wasting the remaining shape\n\nThe developer describes placing blocks into a grid and completing rows or columns for points. The endless format continues until no further placement is possible.\n\nA placement therefore serves two purposes: advancing a potential line and shaping the empty area left for future blocks. An isolated gap may be harder to use than a broader open region, even when both represent the same number of empty cells.\n\nThat is a general implication of the rules, not a tested optimal strategy. The supplied text does not establish rotation, piece-tray size, or a guaranteed solvable sequence. Calling the grid a wooden jigsaw does not mean it assembles a fixed picture.\n\n## Endless runs and timed events are different commitments\n\nThe listing describes high-score competition, a progress chart, challenge modes, and Story Mode with limited-time levels and badges. Those offer different reasons to return.\n\nSomeone who enjoys a self-contained score attempt may not want the same schedule as someone following event rewards. A limited-time event window also does not necessarily mean an individual placement is governed by a countdown.\n\nThe ordinary gameplay is advertised as having no pressure or time limit. No interface inspection establishes the complete scope of that statement across every mode.\n\n## Testimonials are not an independent review sample\n\nThe description contains enthusiastic testimonial-style quotations. No usable customer-review bodies are available separately in this evidence set, so those marketing excerpts are not treated as a player-review digest.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. The developer also discloses in-app purchases and auto-renewing subscriptions lasting one month, six months, or one year. No current prices are supplied in the description.\n\nAdvertising frequency, removal entitlements, offline behavior, and stability remain unverified. The wooden aesthetic and calming pitch do not establish measurable health benefits or an uninterrupted session.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWoody looks most suitable for players who enjoy managing a larger placement grid and deciding between personal scores and event goals. It is less conclusive for someone requiring a particular rotation rule or a fully documented paid-access model. The ten-by-ten format is concrete; the surrounding comfort and economy claims remain attributed.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What board size is described?\nTen by ten.\n\n### Is this a fixed-picture jigsaw?\nNo. The main loop places blocks and clears completed rows or columns.\n\n### Is Story Mode the same as an endless run?\nNo. It is described as limited-time story challenges with badges.\n\n### Are subscription prices verified?\nNo. Durations are listed, but current prices are not supplied here.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/woody-block-puzzle-brain-game/id1212951043?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
