    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Hunt: Swipe for Words Without an Advertised Lives System\n\nWord Hunt · describes a simple word-finding loop with two clear pacing claims: no timers and no lives. Its optional subscription is a separate question from those puzzle rules. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Form the answer through the letters\n\nThe developer describes finding words by swiping letters and earning coins after completing a puzzle. Thousands of puzzles and additional content are advertised.\n\nThat gives the activity a visual entry method rather than a conventional typing interface. Recognizing a word is only part of the task; its letters must also be available to trace in the arrangement.\n\nThe supplied text does not fully explain whether the layout is a grid or another form, whether paths can bend, or whether only straight words are accepted. The title should not be used to import a specific rule set from another app called Word Hunt.\n\n## No lives is a progression claim\n\nThe listing says there are no timers and no lives, positioning the game as an activity that can be continued at the player's pace. Those statements concern waiting and time pressure around ordinary puzzles.\n\nThey do not establish that every hint or booster is free, or that there are no offers between boards. Coins are documented, but their full uses and exchange rates are not.\n\nSomeone who enjoys a word puzzle without managing a life refill may find that relevant. Someone who wants a fully specified dictionary, regional spelling policy, or path rule has less information to compare.\n\n## Weekly subscription, limited regions\n\nThe developer describes an optional weekly subscription available in limited regions. Benefits include removing intrusive ads and banners, plus 400 daily coins and two boosters. The supplied description does not establish a current price or every eligible region.\n\nThe plan auto-renews under its stated terms. It should not be described as a one-time removal purchase or assumed available to every US account simply because the US listing mentions it.\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available in this collection. There is therefore no supported player digest about vocabulary quality, assistance fairness, or actual advertising. The free download is recorded in metadata; offline support and stability remain unverified.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Hunt may suit players who like swiping through letters and prefer a no-lives, no-timer pitch. It is less conclusive for someone selecting on exact path rules or a verified removal offer. The pacing claims are concrete enough to investigate, while the dictionary and subscription availability need direct confirmation.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Are timers advertised?\nThe developer explicitly says there are none.\n\n### Is there a lives system?\nThe listing says no lives and unlimited puzzle play.\n\n### Is the subscription a one-time payment?\nNo. It is described as an auto-renewing weekly plan.\n\n### Is offline play established?\nNo. The supplied description does not document it.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-hunt/id1357352041?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
