    "bodyMarkdown": "# Sticker Book: Color By Number: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nSticker Book: Color By Number replaces tiny painted regions with illustrated pieces. Match stickers to a supplied scene and gradually turn its white gaps into a completed picture.\n\n## Recognize the piece and its destination\n\nThe official image shows a living room with numbered white silhouettes, furniture, and people. A numbered sticker sits in a tray beneath the scene. That supports guided placement rather than drawing every element from scratch.\n\nThe number provides a correspondence cue, while the silhouette supplies visual context. Completing a sofa scene is a different activity from freely arranging furniture in a simulation, despite the promotional decorate-your-room caption.\n\nThe description also mentions choosing themes, backgrounds, and colors. It does not establish the extent of free arrangement, whether a sticker can be rotated, or whether the final composition is predetermined in every mode. The pictured numbered activity is the clearest selection point.\n\n## Supplied art rather than an empty canvas\n\nLandscapes, animals, landmarks, and fantasy worlds are advertised. Their presence suggests variety of subject, not a verified count of available scenes or a guarantee that all categories are free.\n\nCollecting stickers, earning rewards, and unlocking achievements provide surrounding goals. Exact unlock thresholds and the relationship between the collection and ordinary scene completion are not explained.\n\nConsider this format if placing a missing object feels more rewarding than repeatedly tapping small color regions. It is less suitable if you want unrestricted illustration, original composition, or a documented house-design system.\n\n## Calm presentation leaves practical questions\n\nThe developer calls the activity tranquil and suitable for a broad age range. The supplied evidence does not establish a timer policy, wrong-placement penalties, unlimited retries, zoom, or assistance costs. Bright art is not an accessibility test.\n\nThe claims about IQ, concentration, and color therapy are marketing rather than measured benefits. No customer review bodies are available in this sample, so there is no independent player account of difficulty, repetitive scenes, or readable numbering.\n\nThe US download is free. Advertising frequency, optional purchases, removal offers, and offline support remain unresolved. Free access to the app should not be expanded into a promise that every sticker or theme is unrestricted.\n\n## Verdict\n\nSticker Book has a concrete numbered-scene hook, with piece recognition replacing brushwork. Choose it for guided picture completion rather than unverified freedom to design a room or a promise of therapeutic results.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is it freehand drawing?\n\nThe inspected image shows numbered stickers filling matching scene silhouettes, not an empty drawing canvas.\n\n### Can you freely redesign the room?\n\nThe decorate-your-room caption does not establish unrestricted furniture arrangement or simulation controls.\n\n### Is it confirmed untimed?\n\nThe supplied description does not establish the timer or mistake rules.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/sticker-book-color-by-number/id6450409974?uo=4)."
