    "bodyMarkdown": "# Bright Objects・Find the Hidden: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nBright Objects・Find the Hidden makes the size of a search part of the choice. Preview a level’s object count, select a category, and inspect the scene without an advertised timer.\n\n## Not every search uses the same reference\n\nThe developer lists 16 categories. Outlines uses silhouettes and shadows, while 1 by 1 reveals the next target only after finding the current one. Those are meaningful changes to how you identify an object, not merely different background colors.\n\nB&W, Pop Art, Collage, and adventures with a green hero provide visual variety. The official opening image shows an illustrated woman with a magnifier and pictured objects along the bottom. It confirms the search framing without demonstrating every category.\n\nThe listing advertises more than 7,000 levels playable in any order and six new challenges daily. Those are developer scope claims, not an audited count of unique currently accessible scenes.\n\n## Choose a larger search deliberately\n\nLevels contain 15 to 75 objects, with the count shown before starting. Zoom it specifically features 75-object scenes and enlarged exploration. That gives readers a concrete way to distinguish a more extensive search from a smaller checklist.\n\nZoom is especially relevant when a target is small within a detailed picture. Its existence does not independently establish comfortable controls, strong contrast, or readability on every device.\n\nNo timers is explicitly advertised. Mistake penalties, unlimited tapping, and the exact pause or save behavior are not documented, so untimed should not become a promise of entirely consequence-free play.\n\n## Hints and ad removal are recurring benefits\n\nThe supplied description quotes a US monthly subscription of $6.99, including 20 hints and ad removal. This is a listing quote rather than a verified personalized checkout offer. The subscription automatically renews unless disabled before the stated cutoff.\n\nTwenty included hints is not an unlimited-hint promise. The description does not explain every way to earn additional help or precisely which commercial formats removal covers.\n\nThe US download is free. Offline support and present technical behavior remain untested. No customer review bodies are available in this sample to support claims about fair target placement or dependable saving.\n\nConsider Bright Objects if category control, item-count previews, and unhurried inspection appeal. It is less suitable if you want a confirmed one-time unlock or unrestricted assistance without checking the actual offer.\n\n## Verdict\n\nBright Objects offers unusually specific search choices, especially sequential targets and previewed object counts. Its monthly hint allowance is a distinct access decision, not part of a universal free-search guarantee.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can you choose levels out of order?\n\nThe developer explicitly advertises levels playable in any order.\n\n### What is 1 by 1?\n\nIt is a category where finding one object reveals the next target.\n\n### Does the subscription provide unlimited hints?\n\nNo. The listed monthly benefit is 20 hints plus ad removal, not unlimited assistance.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/bright-objects-find-the-hidden/id1542613280?uo=4)."
