    "bodyMarkdown": "# Belt It: Untangle Rope Puzzle: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2022-09-14–2026-10-18 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 2.2–215.10.0. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nBelt It: Untangle Rope Puzzle has a title that can obscure its clearer listed task: position belts to keep cargo secure during transport. The goal is preventing items from falling or colliding.\n\n## Restraint placement is the actual premise\n\nThe description explicitly says to drag and position belts around objects. The official image shows boxes inside an open truck held by a horizontal blue strap.\n\nThat is a cargo-securing problem rather than proof of a conventional knot-untying game. Choosing where a restraint crosses a load can matter more than merely separating two colored cords.\n\nThe supplied text does not establish accurate real-world load physics, a complete test sequence, or safety instruction. This is entertainment, not a guide to securing an actual vehicle load.\n\n## The expected subject can differ from the game\n\nSeveral older reviewers expected a person or test dummy from advertising but encountered boxes instead. Another later account asks for people to return. Those are dated promotional and content-preference reports, not a verified inventory of every current stage.\n\nA supporter enjoys challenging levels and wants more stages. Others find the task easy or repetitive. The sample spans September 2022 through October 2026, so no single level-count report should be relabeled as a current campaign total.\n\n## A strap that returns can interrupt the idea\n\nAn older reviewer says the belt repeatedly returns to its starting position. More recent accounts describe loading freezes or being unable to enter the game. These are reported input and technical problems, not independently reproduced physics defects.\n\nA September supporter still calls it a great game despite glitches. The coexistence of enjoyment and technical frustration matters: disliking the commercial layer does not mean every reviewer rejects the core concept.\n\n## Paid removal has unresolved accounts\n\nSeveral purchasers report continued advertising after paying, including one who says restoration has no effect. Conversely, a 2025 reviewer says they reached level 30 without seeing an ad. That counterpoint prevents a universal ad-frequency claim.\n\nThe US download is free. Historical payment amounts are not treated as current prices, and the scope of any present removal offer remains unverified. One reviewer reports playing without Wi-Fi, but offline support has not been independently tested.\n\nConsider Belt It if figuring out useful restraint placement is appealing. Readers expecting a guaranteed person-buckling mode, deep physical simulation, or interruption-free progression should not assume those from its title or promotion.\n\n## Verdict\n\nBelt It has a more specific cargo-restraint hook than its untangling subtitle suggests. The historical sample’s main qualifications are limited novelty, strap-input complaints, and unresolved ad-removal behavior.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is it mainly about untangling knots?\n\nThe supplied play guide and image emphasize positioning belts to secure cargo.\n\n### Do the reviews establish a current level count?\n\nNo. Older stage-count and repetition reports span several years and versions.\n\n### Are ads reported after payment?\n\nYes, although another account reports no ads through early levels. Present coverage remains unverified.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/belt-it-untangle-rope-puzzle/id1575056736?uo=4)."
