    "bodyMarkdown": "# Offline Games: No WiFi - FunOn: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nOffline Games: No WiFi - FunOn is a collection chosen by activity rather than one continuous campaign. Open a card game, a board contest, or a puzzle depending on the kind of interaction you want.\n\n## The named formats are the useful starting point\n\nThe description specifically includes Ludo, solitaire, block placement, color logic, and match-3. Ludo is described as racing pieces toward a finish against friends or AI, while block puzzles involve fitting shapes and clearing lines.\n\nThat breadth may appeal to a reader who wants several familiar formats without separate downloads. It does not establish that every included variant uses the full rules of a particular tabletop game.\n\nThe supplied text gives no complete inventory of solitaire types, scoring systems, or difficulty settings. A collection label cannot settle those details for each activity.\n\n## Shared-device support is qualified\n\nSolo play, AI opponents, and playing together on one device are advertised where supported. That last phrase matters: it is not a promise that every puzzle includes local multiplayer or that two people can simultaneously control every game.\n\nThe first official image is a promotional globe covered in many game-like icons. It suggests breadth but is not a reliable itemized catalog or demonstration of the navigation interface.\n\nReaders selecting specifically for a two-player trip should inspect the desired game’s local rules rather than assume the whole collection works identically.\n\n## Offline is a strong claim, not a completed test\n\nThe listing repeatedly says the included games work without internet and in airplane mode. That is clearer than vague play-anywhere language, but no offline session was conducted here.\n\nInitial installation, additional content downloads, purchase restoration, and future updates are separate questions. The text does not establish all of their connection needs.\n\nIt also does not promise that every mode is untimed. A collection spanning board games and quick activities may use different clocks or loss conditions, which are not documented in full.\n\n## Access still needs a boundary\n\nThe US download is free. Advertising, purchases, removal offers, and the free-versus-paid catalog are unresolved. Offline capability should not be used to infer that an app never displays ads while connected.\n\nThere are no customer review bodies in this sample. Claims about fast loading, easy navigation, or reliable saves would exceed the evidence.\n\nConsider FunOn for its named assortment and explicit offline proposition. It is less compelling as a recommendation for one precisely specified puzzle or a verified ad-free shared-device experience.\n\n## Verdict\n\nFunOn offers a coherent one-app collection pitch, with unusually explicit airplane-mode language. Its usefulness depends on the exact included activity and access terms, not the sheer number of icons in its promotional image.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is airplane-mode play advertised?\n\nYes. The listing explicitly says the included games work in airplane mode; this was not independently tested.\n\n### Does every game support two people on one device?\n\nNo such universal promise is made. Shared-device support is qualified as available where supported.\n\n### Does offline mean no ads?\n\nNo. Offline claims do not establish connected ad behavior or removal terms.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/offline-games-no-wifi-funon/id6470471626?uo=4)."
