    "bodyMarkdown": "# Magic Cube Puzzle 3D: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nMagic Cube Puzzle 3D turns a twisty puzzle into a virtual object. Restore each face to its initial state, with cube sizes and additional solid shapes supplying different projects.\n\n## Face turns and viewing are different actions\n\nThe listing advertises free rotation of the model around all axes. That lets you inspect another side; it is not the same as freely rearranging stickers or bypassing the puzzle’s legal turns.\n\nThe official image shows a scrambled multi-layer cube, an undo-looking arrow, settings, a time display, and trophy and lock icons. It supports virtual manipulation without demonstrating exact touch gestures or the meaning of every control.\n\nResponsive controls and realistic animation are developer evaluations. No input accuracy, finger reach, or frame-rate assessment was performed here.\n\n## The size range is the concrete attraction\n\nCubes from 2×2×2 through 20×20×20 are advertised, alongside pyramid and dodecahedron puzzles. That makes the app relevant to a reader interested in more than a standard 3×3 model.\n\nThe description does not enumerate every intermediate model, its scramble method, or the availability of each puzzle without unlocking. A broad size range is not proof of a complete lesson course for large cubes.\n\nRestoring larger faces can require managing more pieces, but piece count alone does not establish completion time or a smooth difficulty progression. No supplied review bodies describe that learning experience.\n\n## Solver support has an explicit limit\n\nHints and algorithm guidance through a built-in solver are advertised for the 3×3×3 cube. That qualifier should not be dropped when recommending the app for a much larger model or a different shape.\n\nThe material does not establish camera scanning of a physical cube, manual entry of external states, or optimal move counts. Its clearly supported purpose is a virtual puzzle with specified 3×3 assistance.\n\nAchievements and leaderboards let players share completion time. A visible elapsed clock does not by itself prove a mandatory countdown or a time-limit failure condition.\n\nThe US download is free. Ads, purchases, removal offers, offline support, and content gates remain unresolved. The developer’s claim that the app is free does not independently verify unrestricted access to every size and tool.\n\nConsider Magic Cube for virtual twisting and a large advertised size range. Readers seeking a physical-cube scanner or full solver coverage across all models should not assume either feature.\n\n## Verdict\n\nMagic Cube Puzzle 3D has a specific breadth advantage on paper, especially its large cube sizes. The 3×3-only solver qualification is crucial, keeping assistance expectations separate from the collection’s scale.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What is the largest advertised cube?\n\nThe listing names sizes up to 20×20×20.\n\n### Does the solver cover every shape?\n\nNo. Solver and algorithm guidance are explicitly qualified for the 3×3×3 cube.\n\n### Can it scan a physical cube?\n\nNo camera-input feature is established by the supplied description.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/magic-cube-puzzle-3d/id911550133?uo=4)."
