    "bodyMarkdown": "# Tangled Rope: Solve Puzzles!: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nTangled Rope: Solve Puzzles! puts a knot-like arrangement on a small board and asks you to separate it. Its advertised assistance includes both hints and the option to view a solution.\n\n## Follow a rope through the crossing\n\nThe developer describes dragging, sliding, and moving ropes rather than cutting them. The practical question is how a chosen movement changes the crossings that remain.\n\nThe first official image shows colored ropes stretched between round anchors, several unused-looking circular positions, a hand prompt, a level label, and a 05:00 clock. It supports an anchor-based disentangling presentation.\n\nThat image does not establish how many ropes may share an anchor, whether an endpoint can pass over another rope, or how temporary placements work. Those rules should not be supplied from another rope game with similar art.\n\n## Assistance has two different levels\n\nHints are described as guidance through a difficult spot, while viewing a solution reveals how a puzzle is done. A reader wanting to preserve discovery may value that distinction before opening the stronger form of help.\n\nThe listing does not establish hint prices, refill limits, ad requirements, or whether viewing a solution affects progression. The existence of help is not proof of unlimited free correction.\n\nThe advertised difficulty increases as the tangles grow more intricate. No level count or independently observed progression supports a claim about exactly when demanding knots begin.\n\n## A calming presentation may still have a clock\n\nThe developer promotes a soothing soundtrack and relaxing atmosphere. Those are attributed design intentions rather than a tested audio or stress assessment.\n\nThe visible 05:00 display makes a universal untimed label inappropriate. The supplied text does not clarify whether it is a countdown, a mode-specific limit, or a promotional arrangement.\n\nMove budgets, retry conditions, and penalties also remain undocumented. Calm colors and a simple dragging gesture cannot settle those constraints.\n\n## Select for spatial rearrangement\n\nThe US download is free. Advertising frequency, purchases, removal offers, offline operation, and saving behavior are unresolved. There are no customer review bodies in this sample to verify control reliability or a fair difficulty curve.\n\nConsider Tangled Rope if following connected paths and changing their relative placement sounds engaging. Readers seeking a guaranteed clock-free puzzle or a specific unrestricted anchor system should wait for those exact rules rather than rely on its general relaxation pitch.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTangled Rope presents a clear spatial task and unusually explicit solution-viewing help. Its real limits are not fully described, particularly the clock visible in the official image and the costs attached to assistance.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Do you cut the ropes?\n\nThe listing describes moving and dragging ropes, not a cutting mechanic.\n\n### Can you see a complete solution?\n\nYes. Viewing a solution is advertised separately from hints; access terms are not specified.\n\n### Is it definitely untimed?\n\nNo. The official image shows 05:00, and the supplied text does not explain that clock.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tangled-rope-solve-puzzles/id6599838025?uo=4)."
