    "bodyMarkdown": "# Nuts And Bolts Sort: Read the Size Rule Before Assuming Colors\n\nNuts And Bolts Sort has a familiar name but a particularly important rule in its description: items may be stacked only when their sizes match. A color-sorting guide would go beyond the supplied evidence. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Compatibility and space both matter\n\nThe developer describes tapping a nut or bolt to move it to an adjacent location. The destination must have enough room, and stacked items must match in size.\n\nThose are two separate restrictions. An apparently compatible destination can still be unusable because it lacks capacity. A spacious destination can fail the matching condition. Planning therefore involves preserving useful space, not merely finding a matching item.\n\nThe supplied text does not fully define adjacency, maximum stack height, whether several items move together, or every completed-state requirement. Those details should not be borrowed from a different nut-sorting game.\n\n## Restarting is part of the advertised approach\n\nThe listing explicitly permits restarting without consequences and says there are no harsh penalties or time constraints. That positions the puzzle as something a player can reconsider rather than rush.\n\nA restart is nevertheless different from undoing one action. Only the former is clearly documented here. Someone who wants to reverse a single mistake without rebuilding a plan should not be promised an undo button.\n\nSingle-finger operation is advertised, but that does not independently establish comfortable reach, readable symbols, or practical one-handed use on every device. It is an input claim rather than an accessibility certification.\n\n## The sparse description limits the comparison\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available in the supplied collection. There is no supported player consensus about difficulty, repetition, touch response, or how clearly the size distinctions appear.\n\nNo screenshot was inspected. Consequently, exact colors, thread shapes, and screen layout cannot be used as observed evidence to explain the rules. The safest account follows the written size restriction while noting what it leaves unspecified.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. The supplied text does not establish advertising frequency, removal products, helper prices, offline support, or stability. Saying a restart has no consequences also should not be expanded into a guarantee about every monetization or access condition.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNuts And Bolts Sort is a plausible fit for readers who like organizing compatible stacks while maintaining working space. It is less conclusive for someone choosing specifically for color sorting or detailed recovery controls. The no-timer and restart claims are useful, but the exact stacking implementation still needs direct confirmation.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What matching rule is explicitly stated?\nItems must match in size to stack.\n\n### Is destination space relevant?\nYes. The receiving location must have enough room.\n\n### Is an undo function documented?\nNo. Restarting is advertised, which is not the same feature.\n\n### Is every session verified ad-free?\nNo. The description does not establish advertising behavior.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/nuts-and-bolts-sort/id6470773609?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
