    "bodyMarkdown": "# My Block Puzzle: Endless Scores and a Finite Challenge Collection\n\nMy Block Puzzle offers both a continuing score attempt and individual challenges. Its unusually long review window makes the difference important: finishing a challenge collection is not the same as exhausting an endless score mode. This source-based review combines the US App Store listing with player reports; it is not a hands-on playtest.\n\n## Place carefully because the block stays put\n\nThe listing says to move blocks onto a board, clear complete horizontal or vertical lines, and continue until a new block no longer fits. Once placed, a block cannot be relocated.\n\nNormal mode emphasizes a high score without a time limit. Challenge mode changes board sizes, difficulty, and objectives. The no-time-limit statement should not automatically be expanded to every possible challenge format.\n\nRefresh and rotation appear among subscription benefits, but the description does not establish that those tools are free or unrestricted in every mode.\n\n## Requests for more levels are also evidence of attachment\n\nReviewers in this sample contributed 50 US App Store reviews dated 2020-10-08 through 2026-11-06 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 1.9.8, 2.0.0, 2.0.1, 2.0.2, 2.1.0; the listing records version 2.1.0. Apple's most-recent RSS sample is capped at 50 and self-selected, not representative of all players or a live consensus. These are player reports, not independently verified findings.\n\nReviewers enjoy a relaxing but engaging routine. Many historical accounts say they reached the available content and want additional stages; another reports repeating arrangements under different level numbers.\n\nThose comments span years, not just the current release. They support caution about expecting continual new challenges, but do not independently establish today's exact endpoint or release schedule.\n\nDifficulty reactions also differ. Some appreciate the challenge, while others find it too easy. Old reports of crashes around iOS 14 should not be presented as a new stability finding, although a 2026 reviewer also reports the app not working.\n\n## VIP has a stated recurring cost\n\nThe description lists a weekly VIP plan at $6.99 after a three-day trial, with daily coins, refreshes, and rotations. That is a listing-stated offer, not a newly inspected checkout.\n\nA historical purchaser complains that VIP benefits and ad expectations do not persist. Other accounts range from no annoying ads to frustration over longer breaks. Current removal scope is not established, and the presence of VIP does not independently certify an ad-free session.\n\nA report of smaller coin rewards is similarly not a verified current economy comparison.\n\n## Verdict\n\nMy Block is most relevant to readers who enjoy immovable placements and want both scoring and stage objectives. It is a more cautious choice for someone whose main motivation is a continually expanding challenge collection. The historical sample's attachment is clear, but so are repeated requests for new content and more dependable access.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can a placed block be moved again?\nThe listing says no.\n\n### Is Normal mode timed?\nIt is explicitly described as having no time limit.\n\n### What VIP duration is stated?\nWeekly, with a three-day trial described.\n\n### Are all complaints recent?\nNo. The sample includes accounts dating to 2020.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/my-block-puzzle/id1479855810?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
