    "bodyMarkdown": "# Traffic 3D Parking: The Arrow Sets the Route, You Choose the Order\n\nTraffic 3D Parking describes a traffic puzzle with a concrete instruction: inspect the arrows before moving a car. Its energetic getaway language should not be mistaken for a fully documented racing or steering system. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Choose when a vehicle follows its route\n\nThe developer says a tap sends a car in the direction shown by its arrow. Players assess whether the route is clear, then choose an action order that avoids collisions.\n\nThat places the main decision before movement. A car with a clear exit may create room for a second vehicle, while moving something prematurely can produce a conflict on its route.\n\nThe supplied text does not establish free steering, a brake gesture, whether directions can change, or the penalty for a collision. Those familiar traffic-game features should not be imported from another app.\n\n## Every second counts is not a timer specification\n\nThe description repeatedly emphasizes speed and excitement, but it does not provide a complete countdown rule. Someone specifically looking for an untimed planning game has insufficient evidence for a guarantee either way.\n\nIncreasingly congested levels and new obstacles are advertised. Their actual variety and difficulty curve are not independently evaluated. No screenshot was visually inspected to assess arrow clarity or vehicle spacing.\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available in the supplied collection. There is no supported player digest about touch response, repetition, fairness, or difficulty spikes.\n\n## A weekly premium is separate from coin purchases\n\nThe listing states a premium account without popup ads at $5.99 per week, renewing automatically. It separately lists one-time coin bundles: 10,000 for $1.99, 20,000 for $2.99, and 1,000,000 for $99.99.\n\nThese are description-stated amounts, not a newly inspected checkout. The text itself warns that prices may change. A coin bundle is not a subscription merely because the listing uses a subscription-style heading for purchase duration.\n\nThe no-popup benefit should not expand into a guarantee that every optional reward video disappears. The full relationship between coins, help, and progression is not specified, and no practical ad frequency or offline capability is verified.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTraffic 3D Parking is most relevant to readers who enjoy sequencing arrow-directed vehicles and predicting clear paths. It is less conclusive for someone expecting active steering or a verified no-timer experience. The movement premise is clear, while the distinction between recurring premium and one-time currency deserves equal attention.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What happens when a car is tapped?\nIt follows its indicated direction, according to the listing.\n\n### Is free steering documented?\nNo. The description emphasizes choosing the vehicle and order.\n\n### What is the listed premium duration?\nOne week, with automatic renewal.\n\n### Are the listed prices a verified checkout?\nNo. They are amounts in the supplied description and may change.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/traffic-3d-parking-escape-jam/id6502278761?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
