    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Search Sea: Anagram Letters, Aquarium Rewards, and an Offline Dispute\n\nWord Search Sea sounds like a conventional grid search, but its instructions describe forming words from a circle of letters. Its sample also challenges a claim placed directly in the title: offline access. This source-based review combines the US App Store listing with player reports; it is not a hands-on playtest.\n\n## Generate words rather than scan a large grid\n\nThe developer describes swiping across the given letters in any direction. Correct answers fill a board, bonus words award coins, and answers are listed alphabetically.\n\nThat ordering can provide context when considering a missing answer, although it is not a tested solution strategy for every level. The supplied text does not fully specify letter reuse or the complete bonus-word policy.\n\nAquariums, marine facts, evolution stages, events, and daily crossword-format levels provide progression beyond the immediate word set.\n\n## Approachable vocabulary is not universally satisfying\n\nReviewers in this sample contributed 50 US App Store reviews dated 2026-06-03 through 2026-11-04 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 5.16.03, 5.17.05, 5.18.04, 5.19.08, 5.20.02, 5.21.05, 5.22.02, 5.23.07; the listing records version 5.24.02. Apple's most-recent RSS sample is capped at 50 and self-selected, not representative of all players or a live consensus. These are player reports, not independently verified findings.\n\nPositive reviewers enjoy a calm pace, word building, and the aquarium as a reward. Some find the beginning easy and later arrangements more demanding.\n\nOthers report repeated letter sets or familiar words being rejected. Those are individual dictionary experiences, not an independently audited acceptance policy. The same accessible vocabulary that helps one player unwind can disappoint someone seeking advanced anagrams.\n\nSeveral reviewers also report freezing. These accounts do not establish a current failure rate, but they qualify praise for an otherwise enjoyable routine.\n\n## The title does not settle practical offline access\n\nOffline mode is explicitly advertised. A sampled reviewer says it does not work for them, while the evidence does not resolve the relevant version, preparation, or feature scope through a disconnected test.\n\nAd accounts range from none so far to numerous breaks or videos that cannot be closed. Current removal terms are not established, and one player's tolerance for short ads does not verify every account's schedule.\n\nReferences to survey rewards or PayPal in reviews should not become a promise that the game itself pays cash. Outside reward services have separate, unverified conditions.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Search Sea is most relevant to readers who enjoy approachable anagrams with a marine collection layer. It is a more cautious choice for someone relying on verified offline access or a broad advanced dictionary. The sample supports the cozy progression while preserving specific objections about repetition, accepted words, and interruptions.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Are letters supplied in a circle?\nYes, according to the instructions.\n\n### Is answer ordering documented?\nThe listing says words are listed alphabetically.\n\n### Is offline access independently verified?\nNo. An advertised mode coexists with a contradictory player report.\n\n### Are cash payouts established?\nNo. References to outside reward apps do not verify a payout program.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-search-sea-offline-games/id1245180154?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
