    "bodyMarkdown": "# Word Wiz - Connect Words Game: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2023-12-21–2026-06-18 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 2.17–2.23.0. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nWord Wiz - Connect Words Game offers a small pool of letters and asks how many answers you can build. The useful distinction is word construction, not searching for already printed answers in a dense grid.\n\n## A wheel feeds the answer spaces\n\nThe official image shows FAIR being traced from a circular letter pool, with related answers above. The developer advertises more than 10,000 puzzles, a dictionary, and relaxing or challenge modes.\n\nThose are listing claims rather than a complete dictionary audit. One detailed reviewer enjoys puzzles that are challenging without being impossible, but says some ordinary words are not accepted as bonuses.\n\nAnother likes encountering words they have not heard before. These accounts support vocabulary discovery as an attraction without proving measurable language improvement.\n\n## Changes can remove a reason to return\n\nA January 2026 reviewer misses earning a daily letter toward an unfamiliar word; another asks where the vocabulary builder went. Their loss matters because discovering a word can be a different reward from simply filling the grid.\n\nAn older reviewer also says the difficult option disappeared. That conflicts with the advertised mode choice without establishing what every current account can access.\n\nThe sample spans December 2023 through June 2026. It should not be read as a single current update cycle or proof that every historical interface remains unchanged.\n\n## A repair is not a universal clean bill\n\nA September 2024 reviewer thanks the team for fixing a freeze when earning a crown. Earlier detailed accounts describe that specific animation blocking progress.\n\nLater reviews still report other crashes and ads that will not close. Keeping the acknowledged crown repair does not require treating every subsequent technical complaint as resolved.\n\nOne reviewer discusses suspected bot opponents, but that account does not independently establish this app’s matchmaking architecture. The wheel-and-grid task is better documented than that isolated competition description.\n\n## Commercials can interrupt forming the word\n\nMultiple historical reviews describe pop-ups covering letters during a swipe, not just between puzzles. Others tolerate short ads while disliking crashes. Reported intervals vary and were not timed here.\n\nThe US download is free. A request for a paid edition is not proof that removal is currently unavailable, and present purchase coverage remains unresolved. Offline operation and save restoration were not tested.\n\nConsider Word Wiz if a compact anagram pool and dictionary progression are appealing, while checking whether the learning features that interest you are actually present.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWord Wiz has specific supporters of approachable word finding. The historical evidence makes feature continuity and mid-puzzle interruptions more useful selection questions than its broad brain-training language.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is it a conventional word-search grid?\n\nThe inspected example instead connects a small circular letter pool into answer spaces.\n\n### Was a crown freeze ever reported fixed?\n\nYes. One September 2024 reviewer explicitly thanks the team for that repair; other later issues remain separate.\n\n### Are both advertised difficulty modes confirmed now?\n\nNo. An older reviewer reports the harder option missing, and current account access was not tested.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/word-wiz-connect-words-game/id1462123372?uo=4)."
