    "bodyMarkdown": "# Parking Master 3D Car Parking: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2024-08-21–2026-10-22 (Asia/Shanghai), covering versions 2.2.5–2.3.6. This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nParking Master 3D Car Parking asks which vehicle can leave a congested lot without hitting obstacles or pedestrians. Its advertised city-building layer gives earned currency another purpose outside the parking board.\n\n## Departure order is the central decision\n\nThe developer describes swiping cars left or right and choosing a workable release sequence. Grannies and cops complicate the perimeter, while Hero mode gives emergency vehicles priority.\n\nThe official image shows a tightly packed lot beneath a 45-move display. Boss levels are explicitly described as timed, so the app should not receive a universal untimed label.\n\nA supporter likes a challenge that keeps them occupied without becoming frustrating. Another still enjoys ordinary boards but finds the separate challenges too demanding. Those are mode preferences rather than proof of one consistent difficulty curve.\n\n## Small targets and direction are different concerns\n\nAn older reviewer finds cars too small to identify their orientation or select accurately. A March 2026 account says a forward gesture sends a car backward, then reports crashing near completion.\n\nThose are unverified visibility and input reports. They do not establish deliberate collisions or an audited cause of lost moves.\n\nA separate launch complaint explicitly mentions a damaged iPad as a possible reason. It should not be converted into an independently confirmed app-only defect.\n\n## The city can run out of purpose\n\nMultiple historical reviewers accumulate money but cannot reach a coastal city or find new construction. One continues parking while questioning why the earned currency has nowhere useful to go.\n\nThat matters if city growth is the reason to keep clearing lots. It does not prove a present maximum level or establish that no content update ever occurred.\n\nThe sample spans August 2024 through October 2026. Historical city-access reports are not a current exhaustive campaign inventory.\n\n## Advertising can cover the cars\n\nA detailed reviewer reports ads over the play area during active movement. Others describe long between-board videos or needing ads for skins and construction despite surplus coins.\n\nA contrasting account says there are fewer ads than expected. The conflict prevents a measured universal schedule, while allegations about misleading promotions remain attributed.\n\nThe US download is free. Current purchases, removal terms, offline play, and save transfer remain unresolved; one reviewer reports losing progress on a new phone.\n\nConsider Parking Master for release-order puzzles, but treat legible targets, city expansion, and mode access as important questions rather than assuming the promotional lot is the whole experience.\n\n## Verdict\n\nParking Master has a clear traffic-release premise with supporters of its moderate ordinary challenge. Historical city dead ends and active-play obstructions are more specific concerns than simply saying it contains ads.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Are any modes timed?\n\nYes. The listing explicitly describes Boss levels with limited time.\n\n### Is the city expansion fully verified?\n\nNo. Several reviewers report inaccessible later construction or accumulated currency without uses.\n\n### Are all launch problems proven app defects?\n\nNo. One reviewer explicitly says a damaged device may explain their own problem.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/parking-master-3d-car-parking/id6444550569?uo=4)."
