    "bodyMarkdown": "# Crostic Crossword－Word Puzzles: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nCrostic Crossword－Word Puzzles makes one solved word useful in several places. Numbered letters connect clue answers to a hidden quote or phrase, so progress is shared across the puzzle.\n\n## Clues and code work together\n\nThe developer explains that the same number always means the same letter within a puzzle. Entering an answer automatically places matching letters elsewhere, including in the hidden message.\n\nThat creates two routes into a difficult clue. Solve another answer to expose letters, or recognize part of the message and use those letters to revisit the clue.\n\nThis is not merely a traditional crossword grid with decorative numbers. The cross-reference system supplies the connections that physical crossing cells provide in an ordinary crossword.\n\n## A phrase is also a source of deductions\n\nQuotes, proverbs, and unexpected phrases are advertised, followed by related facts after completion. Recognizing an expression may help before every clue is solved.\n\nThe listing does not establish the accuracy, attribution, or source coverage of all facts and quotations. A code puzzle can supply interesting reading without becoming a verified reference database.\n\nThe official image shows a numbered notebook-style layout, pictured clue icons, and promotional claims of 32,000+ questions and 3,200 levels. Those counts are not independently audited and do not establish that every board is freely available.\n\n## The daily activities are named separately\n\nA Daily Challenge offers points and a daily leaderboard. Daily Levels instead mention distinct puzzles and collectible trophies. The two labels should not be collapsed into a single verified mode with identical scoring.\n\nHelpful hints are advertised without a full allowance or price schedule. The description does not define mistake limits, letter-entry penalties, or whether a difficult clue can be skipped indefinitely.\n\nPlay-at-your-own-pace language does not independently establish the absence of a clock in every competitive daily activity. Current mode rules were not tested.\n\n## Recurring access lacks a quoted offer\n\nThe US download is free. The subscription paragraph describes automatic renewal and trial terms but does not provide a concrete current price, cadence, or complete entitlement list in the supplied text.\n\nAdvertising, paid removal, offline access, and save reliability remain unresolved. There are no customer review bodies here to support claims about clue quality or fair hints.\n\nConsider Crostic for its clear two-way connection between answers and message. Readers who prefer complete independence between clues or need a confirmed unrestricted catalog should not assume either.\n\n## Verdict\n\nCrostic has a specific decoding proposition: every correct letter can help multiple answers and the hidden phrase. Its daily structure is documented, while accuracy, commercial access, and practical assistance limits remain unverified.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Does a number keep the same letter?\n\nYes, within a puzzle according to the developer.\n\n### Can the phrase help with a clue?\n\nYes. The described connections work both from solved answers to the phrase and from recognized phrase letters back to answers.\n\n### Is a subscription price established?\n\nNo. Renewal terms are included, but the supplied description does not state a concrete current offer.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/crostic-crossword-word-puzzles/id1636821805?uo=4)."
