    "bodyMarkdown": "# Cross-Stitch: Coloring Book: Player Review Analysis\n\n*Player-review analysis, not a playtest. Sources: the US App Store listing and 50 US reviews dated 2023-05-28–2026-10-05 (Asia/Shanghai), covering multiple raw version labels (inconsistent formats) . This limited, self-selected sample is not representative; player reports are not independently verified.*\n\nCross-Stitch: Coloring Book translates embroidery into a coded picture grid. Follow letters and numbers to fill stitches, or use the advertised image-import feature to convert a personal photo into a pattern.\n\n## The coded grid is the central activity\n\nThe official image shows a dog assembled from small colored stitch-like cells, with a lettered palette and tool icons below. This is guided completion rather than drawing a new composition freely.\n\nA detailed supporter likes the range of patterns and finds this easier than other cross-stitch apps. Another values bright colors and relaxation. These are reasons to enjoy the activity, not proof of a therapeutic effect.\n\nThe listing names animals, flowers, mystery, seasonal designs, and more. It does not establish that every pattern or import setting is free.\n\n## Moving the picture can make the wrong stitch\n\nOne reviewer says panning accidentally places stitches. Another describes a grid that moves or zooms unexpectedly and requests a lock.\n\nThose are unverified input complaints, but they concern the repeated action itself. A small mistake is not automatically harmless if navigation and painting are difficult to separate.\n\nAn older reviewer reports that an incorrect stitch cannot be undone. Current correction tools were not tested, so that claim should not be generalized into a complete present-day rulebook.\n\n## Daily art is an unsettled promise\n\nThe developer advertises daily updates. Several 2026 reviewers instead report weeks without new daily pictures, including a yearly payer who sees no new items.\n\nAn earlier reviewer distinguishes an ad-removal purchase from VIP and says the free catalog is exhausted. That is a useful reminder that removing commercials and unlocking patterns may be different entitlements.\n\nPhoto import is also a concrete attraction, but a 2023 yearly subscriber says it stopped working. Other requests for better import do not establish a verified current repair.\n\n## Recovery can have a cost\n\nA January 2025 reviewer says reinstallation fixed a glitch but removed membership boosters. That is a partial recovery account, not either total failure or a completely restored experience.\n\nOther reviewers describe pop-ups over a picture and forced ads after declining a reward multiplier. Advertising frequency, current prices, removal coverage, and offline support remain unresolved.\n\nThe US download is free. The sample spans May 2023 through October 2026, and its inconsistent raw version labels remain preserved in the source notes. Consider this app for coded imagery and imports, with content renewal and reliable grid movement as practical priorities.\n\n## Verdict\n\nCross-Stitch has specific supporters of its patterns and easy entry. Missing new art, input separation, and the difference between ad removal and catalog membership are the strongest qualifications in the historical sample.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can personal photos become patterns?\n\nThe listing advertises that feature, although an older subscriber reports import trouble.\n\n### Does ad removal unlock every pattern?\n\nThat is not established. One reviewer explicitly distinguishes their removal purchase from VIP access.\n\n### Did reinstallation restore everything for the reported user?\n\nNo. They say the glitch cleared but collected membership boosters were lost.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cross-stitch-coloring-book/id1499339385?uo=4)."
