    "bodyMarkdown": "# Jigsaw Puzzles: Puzzle Game HD: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nJigsaw Puzzles: Puzzle Game HD offers the familiar picture-completion task: drag loose pieces into their corresponding positions until the supplied image is whole.\n\n## The picture supplies both target and reward\n\nThe listing names nature, landmarks, art, animals, and flowers. Subject selection is meaningful because recognizing a coastline or pet can help organize the visual search as well as make the finished result appealing.\n\nThe official image shows a lake-and-trees picture inside a phone, with visible joins, loose pieces beneath, and a floating piece being moved. It supports digital assembly rather than coloring numbered regions.\n\nNo full-size puzzle was completed here. Snap tolerance, accidental placement, sorting trays, and the visibility of the source image remain untested.\n\n## Piece count is the stated difficulty lever\n\nThe developer describes three difficulty levels and an adjustable range of 36–100 pieces. Elsewhere the same text says puzzles can contain hundreds of pieces.\n\nThat discrepancy should not be resolved by inventing a maximum. The specifically stated range is useful source information, while the broader scale claim remains unverified.\n\nMore pieces can divide an image into smaller cues, but the actual demand also depends on artwork and assistance. No hands-on finding establishes a steady difficulty curve or exact completion times.\n\n## Familiar jigsaw questions remain open\n\nThe supplied text does not explain rotation, edge-only filters, background guides, automatic sorting, or whether pieces must be joined in one fixed order.\n\nThose features often shape a digital jigsaw experience, but their absence from the description is not proof that they do not exist. It is simply insufficient evidence to recommend the app for one of them.\n\nA claim of daily new free pictures is also not an independently audited update schedule. Current free access to each category or difficulty was not checked.\n\n## Offline is advertised, therapy is not established\n\nThe developer explicitly says the game works without internet. It does not fully define whether every future picture must first be downloaded or which connected features remain available.\n\nThe text associates fifteen minutes of daily play with reduced anxiety and sharper thinking. No clinical evidence or measured outcome is supplied for that prescription, and the analysis does not adopt it.\n\nThe US download is free. Ads, purchases, removal offers, saving behavior, and current stability remain unresolved. No customer review bodies are available here to confirm them.\n\nConsider this app for picture assembly and its stated piece-count choice, while checking the exact maximum and any sorting aids rather than assuming a complete physical-jigsaw toolkit.\n\n## Verdict\n\nThis jigsaw listing communicates a recognizable task and useful image categories. Its conflicting piece-count language and undocumented assembly aids limit a more precise recommendation.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What piece range is specifically stated?\n\nThe feature list says 36–100, while other wording claims hundreds; the discrepancy remains unresolved.\n\n### Can pieces rotate?\n\nThe supplied material does not establish rotation rules.\n\n### Is offline play advertised?\n\nYes, without independently tested download boundaries or disconnected behavior.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/jigsaw-puzzles-puzzle-game-hd/id1611547216?uo=4)."
