    "bodyMarkdown": "# Wooden Puzzle Bliss: iOS Listing Analysis\n\n*Store-listing analysis, not a playtest. This article examines the US App Store description and attributed product claims. Customer review sample: N=0; no review date or version window is available.*\n\nWooden Puzzle Bliss uses shaped blocks and a grid, despite calling itself a jigsaw in the promotional text. The explicitly stated task is making lines while avoiding a completely congested board.\n\n## Fit shapes, then open room\n\nThe developer describes connecting blocks and shapes, forming lines, and paying attention not to fill the whole grid. Color matching and match-3 are explicitly excluded.\n\nThe official image shows a partially occupied wood-toned board, a highlighted shape, three piece slots, score and trophy displays, and assistance icons beneath.\n\nThat supports placement and space management rather than reconstructing a supplied photograph. The jigsaw comparison should not become a claim that every block has one predetermined final position.\n\n## The next footprint matters\n\nA placement can be useful because it completes a line or because it leaves an area broad enough for another shape. The source does not independently establish which scoring choice is optimal.\n\nIt also does not fully define rows versus columns, piece rotation, batch replacement, or a guaranteed-solvable generator. Familiar block-game conventions are not a complete rulebook for this app.\n\nThe pictured three slots show available pieces, not proof that every new set arrives only after all three are placed. The exact refresh rule is unresolved.\n\n## No clock is a stated distinction\n\nThe listing explicitly says no time limit and invites readers to start and resume whenever desired. That supports deliberate placement as an intended format.\n\nResumption remains a developer promise rather than a save-reliability test. It does not establish cloud transfer, recovery after deletion, or whether a completed high score is synchronized between devices.\n\nThe tool icons have numeric counters in the image, but their exact effects, refill conditions, and costs are not supplied. They should not be labeled unlimited undo or free bombs merely from their appearance.\n\n## Bliss is not a clinical finding\n\nThe developer associates the game with a healthy brain, reduced stress, and increased happiness. No measured health outcome or controlled study is supplied for those claims.\n\nThere are no customer review bodies here to establish how satisfying the placement feels, whether pieces repeat, or how interruption-free an ordinary run is.\n\nThe US download is free. Advertising frequency, purchases, removal benefits, offline access, and present stability remain unresolved. Completely free wording does not independently settle every commercial offer.\n\nConsider Wooden Puzzle Bliss for a wood-grid line-making task without an advertised timer. Readers wanting a picture jigsaw or a verified ad-free concentration space should not infer either from its name and calming pitch.\n\n## Verdict\n\nWooden Puzzle Bliss explains line formation more clearly than its jigsaw label suggests. Its no-time-limit and resume claims are useful on paper, while piece rules, tool costs, and actual commercial interruptions remain open.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is it assembling a picture jigsaw?\n\nThe stronger written instruction and inspected image show block placement to form lines.\n\n### Does color determine clearing?\n\nNo. The listing explicitly says no color matching or match-3.\n\n### Are offline saves verified?\n\nNo. Resume is advertised, but disconnected operation and save reliability were not tested.\n\n[US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/wooden-puzzle-bliss/id6446890186?uo=4)."
