    "bodyMarkdown": "# Traffic Jam Fever: A Road-Drawing Premise With Sparse Rules\n\nTraffic Jam Fever has an unusually brief store description: draw new roads so more vehicles can pass without creating traffic. That identifies a traffic-flow idea, but not a complete puzzle rulebook. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Roads are the documented intervention\n\nThe published action is drawing roads. It should not be confused with tapping parked cars out along fixed arrows or steering each car directly through a parking lot.\n\nThe stated goal is improving vehicle passage while avoiding congestion. The description does not explain the drawing gesture, available connection points, construction limits, or how success is measured.\n\nLikewise, no road budget, collision penalty, countdown, or exact throughput target is documented. A familiar traffic theme is not enough to establish those rules.\n\n## Planning a network is a different interest\n\nThe premise may interest readers who like deciding where connections belong rather than finding one car's escape sequence. That is an interpretation of the documented action, not a claim about a tested simulation.\n\nSomeone specifically seeking realistic traffic modeling, editable intersections, or a sandbox has too little evidence here. None of those features is established by the single-sentence pitch.\n\nNo screenshot was visually inspected. Actual road shapes, vehicle scale, camera view, and interface controls are therefore not described as observations.\n\n## Access and feedback are also unknown\n\nNo usable customer-review bodies are available in the supplied evidence. There is no supported player verdict on the difficulty curve, congestion behavior, advertising, or reliability.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. It does not establish removal pricing, offline support, unlimited play, or the absence of paid tools. These are evidence limits rather than claims that a particular feature is missing.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTraffic Jam Fever is identifiable as a road-drawing candidate, but the source is too thin for a detailed strategy or a strong usability recommendation. It is relevant to an interest in traffic flow, not a confirmed substitute for a particular parking puzzle or realistic road simulator.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What action is explicitly described?\nDrawing new roads.\n\n### Is this confirmed as a parking-exit game?\nNo. That is not the stated action.\n\n### Are budgets or timers documented?\nNo. The supplied description does not give those rules.\n\n### Are player opinions available here?\nNo usable review bodies are supplied.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/traffic-jam-fever/id1659370477?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
