    "bodyMarkdown": "# Art Ball 3D: Collect Color Before Sending It to the Canvas\n\nArt Ball 3D connects moving a ball with making a painting. Its short description establishes a collect-and-dispatch idea, but leaves the detailed puzzle rules largely unexplained. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Movement supplies the paint\n\nThe developer says moving a finger moves the ball, with colored spheres gathering around it. Those colors are then dispatched to a canvas.\n\nThat is different from directly selecting numbered regions in a coloring book. The published action begins with movement and collection rather than individually filling an illustrated outline.\n\nThe description does not explain whether color order matters, whether collection is selective, or how dispatching is triggered. A rule requiring every gathered sphere to match one target color would be an invention.\n\n## Art is the destination, not necessarily a drawing studio\n\nPainting provides the described payoff for collecting. That may interest readers who like converting a movement task into a completed image.\n\nIt does not establish freehand creation, photo import, unrestricted color choice, or export tools. Likewise, a ball moving through an area does not prove collision hazards, a runner course, or a countdown.\n\nThose are missing details, not negative findings about the app. The source is simply too brief to identify the complete skill test or the exact failure condition.\n\nNo screenshot was inspected. Actual arena shape, paint style, ball scale, and canvas layout are not described as observed facts.\n\n## Free access remains a separate question\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available in the supplied evidence. There is no supported player consensus about responsiveness, repetition, difficulty, or the pleasure of finishing a canvas.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. It does not establish ad frequency, paid removal, offline operation, helper costs, or stability. A simple two-sentence premise should not be translated into a promise of a simple payment model.\n\n## Verdict\n\nArt Ball 3D is relevant to an interest in movement-based color collection, not a confirmed substitute for a conventional painting editor. The collect-to-canvas loop is identifiable; its planning depth and access conditions are not. A stronger recommendation would need more detailed rules or direct observation.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### How is the ball moved?\nThe listing says to move a finger on screen.\n\n### What gets collected?\nColored spheres, according to the description.\n\n### Is freehand drawing established?\nNo. The source describes dispatching collected colors.\n\n### Are hazards or timers documented?\nNo. Neither is stated in the supplied description.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/art-ball-3d-canvas-puzzle/id1478273910?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
