    "bodyMarkdown": "# Midas Merge: Three-of-a-Kind Growth and Sunlit Garden Recovery\n\nMidas Merge gives merging a visible purpose: restore the Gardens of Gold after a shattered crown leaves the land in darkness. Its most specific loop links creatures, harvested fruit, and Sunbursts that uncover more of the garden. This source-based analysis uses the US App Store listing, not hands-on play.\n\n## Three or more becomes something new\n\nThe developer says to drag and match at least three objects of a kind to evolve them. Creatures hatch from eggs, develop through collection, and help harvest items.\n\nFruit shrubs contribute toward Sunbursts. Tapping those produces Sun that banishes darkness and opens the garden. That is a more defined chain than simply combining objects for a higher number.\n\nThe description does not state an exact five-item bonus formula, every merge-chain length, or a universal rule for recovering an accidental combination. Those details should not be imported from other merge games.\n\n## A garden with several linked goals\n\nQuests support hatching a Guardian Creature and obtaining rarer treasures. Hearts help repair damaged landmarks, while organizing items and merging supplies supports broader restoration.\n\nA Vault of Riches mini-game offers items to bring back to the garden. The text does not explain its complete probability system or every participation condition.\n\nReferences to coins, riches, and prizes describe the fantasy economy. They do not establish real-money earnings, withdrawable balances, or a cash competition.\n\n## Collection and organization may appeal differently\n\nA reader who enjoys building several related collections may find the mixture of creatures, objects, and restored landmarks appealing. Someone who wants a compact puzzle with a clearly stated ending may prefer firmer information about garden scope and progression.\n\nThe source promises organizational freedom but does not fully document storage limits, creature stamina, or session gates. None should be invented, whether as praise for generosity or criticism of waiting.\n\nNo screenshot was inspected. Specific creature designs, landscape details, or interface arrangement are therefore not described as firsthand observations.\n\n## Access is less detailed than the merge loop\n\nNo customer-review bodies are available in the supplied evidence. There is no supported player verdict about pacing, event pressure, fairness, or repetition.\n\nThe metadata records a free download. Advertising frequency, removal offers, paid-item conditions, offline support, and stability remain unverified. The relaxing title is not independent proof of untimed or unrestricted operation.\n\n## Verdict\n\nMidas Merge looks relevant to readers who enjoy combining a growing collection into a larger restoration project. It is less conclusive for someone needing a known session economy or precise bonus formula. Its documented strength is the connected merge-harvest-Sun loop, not a verified promise of unlimited progress.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### What is the advertised minimum merge?\nThree matching objects.\n\n### What do Sunbursts do?\nThey produce Sun used to banish darkness.\n\n### Is a five-merge bonus documented?\nNo exact bonus rule is given.\n\n### Are the Vault's prizes real cash?\nNo real-money reward program is established by the description.\n\n[View the official US App Store listing](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/midas-merge-relaxing-games/id1641784744?uo=4) · [How evidence differs from playtesting](https://puzzlereviewlab.com/how-we-test/)"
